WaterOptions`, `WaterSurface`, `Wfc`, `WfcOptions`, `WfcTile`, `WindUniforms`, `woodMaterial`\n\n## 1. Engine and games\n5:## Sections\n23:## 1. Engine and games\n542:## 2. Camera\n677:## 3. Rendering, looks and filters\n1146:## 4. Materials, meshes and lights\n1387:## 5. Physics\n2132:## 6. Characters\n2240:## 7. Input and touch\n2452:## 8. Audio\n2668:## 9. Particles\n2760:## 10. HUD\n2820:## 11. Models and textures (ASSETS.md)\n3539:## 12. Animation toolkit\n3852:## 13. Hero kit\n3895:## 14. three.js and Rapier\n3909:## 15. More\n\n11:5. Physics: `BoxOptions`, `Breakable`, `BreakableOptions`, `Breakables`, `BridgeOptions`, `Built`, `chain`, `ChainOptions`, `CharacterAnim`, `CharacterController`, `CharacterOptions`, `Chunk`, `clothGrid`, `ClothOptions`, `Crumble`, `CrumbleOptions`, `DoorOptions`, `DriveInput`, `explode`, `ExplosionOptions`, `Field`, `fieldAcceleration`, `FieldOptions`, `FIXED_DT`, `FloaterOptions`, `Floaters`, `ForceFields`, `fractureBox`, `FractureOptions`, `hingeDoor`, `InstancedBodies`, `InstancedBodiesOptions`, `InstancedShape`, `KinematicBody`, `Mover`, `MoverOptions`, `moverRotation`, `Movers`, `orbit`, `pathPoint`, `pendulum`, `Physics`, `PhysicsState`, `Ragdoll`, `RagdollOptions`, `RagdollPart`, `Rewind`, `RewindOptions`, `RippleField`, `RippleOptions`, `ropeBridge`, `ropeLine`, `seeded`, `seesaw`, `SeesawOptions`, `softBlob`, `springPad`, `SpringPadOptions`, `Trigger`, `TriggerOptions`, `TriggerShape`, `Vehicle`, `VehicleOptions`, `VerletBody`, `VerletOptions`, `waterHeight`, `WaterWave`, `WAVES_CALM`, `WAVES_CHOPPY`\n13:7. Input and touch: `applyDeadzone`, `ButtonEvent`, `DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS`, `GAMEPAD_BUTTONS`, `GamepadLike`, `Input`, `InputFrame`, `InputState`, `MOUSE_BUTTONS`, `PRESS_WINDOW`, `TOUCH_KEY`, `TouchButton`, `TouchButtonState`, `TouchControls`, `TouchCorner`\n220:- `settings?: { button?: TouchCorner | boolean; key?: string | false }`: The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate, sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true: 'top-right'; on a mouse it shows while the pointer moves), or false for n…\n221:- `touch?: boolean`: On-screen joystick + buttons. Default: auto (coarse pointer), or ?touch=1 / ?touch=0.\n309:- `viewport?: Viewport`: The viewport the art resolution and framing come from, as a page's would (default 960×540 at DPR 1). Pointer aim and HUD layout depend on it: a replay uses its recording's (`Recording.view`).\n594:- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit direction. For picking things with the mouse, or aiming at it. An orthographic rig stands far b…\n625:Eyes of the character: mouse look (click to lock the pointer) or Q/E to turn. No zoom.\n1421:- `readonly tiles: Crumble[]`\n1428:- `crumble(o: CrumbleOptions): Crumble`: A floor tile that drops shortly after you step on it, and grows back.\n1543:### interface Crumble\n1545:- `readonly o: CrumbleOptions`\n1551:### interface CrumbleOptions\n2253:A pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates).\n2268:### GAMEPAD_BUTTONS\n2271:const GAMEPAD_BUTTONS: Readonly<Record<number, string>>\n2274:Standard-mapping gamepad buttons → the key codes they press (see character/controls.ts\n2275:KEYMAP). Change `input.gamepadButtons` to remap. Indices follow the W3C \"standard\" layout:\n2278:### interface GamepadLike\n2280:The parts of the Gamepad API that Input reads (tests can pass plain objects).\n2289:Keyboard + pointer + gamepad input.\n2292:- Gamepads (standard mapping): the left stick feeds `moveAxis()` (radial deadzone), the\n2293:  right stick feeds the pointer delta (camera look), buttons press key codes\n2294:  (`gamepadButtons`). Polled once per frame by the engine (`beginFrame`).\n2295:- Pointer: accumulated movement per frame (while a button is held or the pointer is\n2296:  locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\n2303:- `readonly mouseDelta: { x: number; y: number; }`: Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock).\n2304:- `readonly pointer: { x: number; y: number; over: boolean; touch: boolean; }`: Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up: `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now. Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\n2306:- `wantsPointerLock: boolean`: When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera).\n2308:- `readonly padAxis: { x: number; y: number; }`: Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward).\n2309:- `gamepadConnected: boolean`: True while any gamepad is connected.\n2311:- `gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>`: Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS).\n2312:- `gamepadDeadzone: number`: Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1).\n2313:- `gamepadLookSpeed: number`: Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt.\n2315:- `get playing: boolean`: True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events, `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send` are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\n2317:- `attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void`: Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\n2319:- `release(): void`: Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay.\n2320:- `reset(): void`: Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads).\n2321:- `beginFrame(now: number, dt: number, pads?: readonly (GamepadLike | null)[]): void`: Engine: begin a frame at game time `now` (seconds). Polls gamepads and drops expired queued presses. `pads` defaults to `navigator.getGamepads()`; tests can pass fakes.\n2328:- `state(): InputState`: Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames.\n2332:- `moveAxis(): { x: number; y: number }`: -1..1 on each axis (x = right, y = forward): the touch joystick or a gamepad's left stick (whichever is tilted further), else WASD / arrow keys / d-pad.\n2335:- `setPointer(x: number, y: number, down?: boolean): void`: Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not.\n2338:- `get buttonEvents: readonly ButtonEvent[]`: This frame's pointer button presses and releases, in order, each with where the pointer was: a drag shorter than a frame (a script's) still starts where it started and ends where it ended. Recorded with the frame. UI that acts on clicks reads these; play read…\n2342:- `addPointer(dx: number, dy: number, wheel = 0): void`: Test hook: inject pointer movement / wheel for the next frame.\n2343:- `snapshot(dt: number, last?: SnapshotMemory): InputFrame`: This frame's input as data (after `beginFrame`), for a recording. `last` is the frame before: unchanged held keys, pointer and gamepad connection are left out.\n2345:- `playAfter(f: InputFrame): void`: Replay, after `beginFrame` (which polled no gamepads): sticks, pointer, wheel, gamepad connection.\n2350:Optional fields are left out when empty or zero; `held` and `pointer` also when unchanged\n2354:- `held?: string[]`: Keys held, keyboard and gamepad buttons together, sorted.\n2356:- `analog?: [number, number]`: The touch joystick and the gamepad's left stick (after its deadzone).\n2358:- `delta?: [number, number]`: Pointer movement (CSS pixels) and wheel ticks this frame.\n2360:- `pointer?: [number, number, number, number]`: Pointer position (normalised device coordinates), over the canvas (1/0), buttons (`mouseButtons`: what `held` says).\n2361:- `gamepad?: boolean`: Whether a gamepad is connected (`gamepadConnected`), when that changes.\n2362:- `touch?: boolean`: Whether the pointer is a touch (`pointer.touch`), when that changes.\n2363:- `clicks?: [string, 0 | 1, number, number][]`: Pointer buttons pressed (1) and let go (0) this frame, in order, each where the pointer was (`buttonEvents`).\n2369:What input a later frame still reads, as data (`engine.snapshot()`): keys held, presses not yet used and how old they are, the pointer.\n2373:- `readonly pointer: readonly [number, number, number, number]`\n2374:- `readonly gamepad: boolean`\n2429:Camera: drag on the game to orbit/look, pinch to zoom (handled by Input.attachPointer).\n2469:first key / pointer / touch input. Before that, and wherever Web Audio does not exist\n2609:- `vibrato?: { depth: number; rate: number }`: Vibrato depth in semitones and rate in Hz.\n4617:- `readonly view?: Viewport`: The viewport it was recorded on, as it was when the level began (CSS pixels and DPR): the art resolution, pointer aim and the HUD's layout follow it. A headless replay frames for it; a page warns when its own differs. A page resized during the level is not fo…","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"b15fd9c6-657a-4416-92fa-b99b0040296c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:23.197Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Pixel Engine API (v0.46.0)\n\nEvery export of `pixel-engine.js` (493 names), generated from the engine's TypeScript at build 2026-11-02 f75d4a6. Signatures are the source declarations; descriptions are their doc comments. Read GUIDE.md first: it says how the pieces fit; come here for exact names and parameters (search this file, don't read it whole).\n\n## Sections\n\n1. Engine and games: `ADAPTIVE_ASPECT`, `AspectMode`, `BUILTIN_MODELS`, `chunkyResolution`, `clearScene`, `computeFraming`, `count