olean): void`: Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not.\n2338:- `get buttonEvents: readonly ButtonEvent[]`: This frame's pointer button presses and releases, in order, each with where the pointer was: a drag shorter than a frame (a script's) still starts where it started and ends where it ended. Recorded with the frame. UI that acts on clicks reads these; play read…\n2342:- `addPointer(dx: number, dy: number, wheel = 0): void`: Test hook: inject pointer movement / wheel for the next frame.\n2343:- `snapshot(dt: number, last?: SnapshotMemory): InputFrame`: This frame's input as data (after `beginFrame`), for a recording. `last` is the frame before: unchanged held keys, pointer and gamepad connection are left out.\n2345:- `playAfter(f: InputFrame): void`: Replay, after `beginFrame` (which polled no gamepads): sticks, pointer, wheel, gamepad connection.\n2350:Optional fields are left out when empty or zero; `held` and `pointer` also when unchanged\n2354:- `held?: string[]`: Keys held, keyboard and gamepad buttons together, sorted.\n2356:- `analog?: [number, number]`: The touch joystick and the gamepad's left stick (after its deadzone).\n2358:- `delta?: [number, number]`: Pointer movement (CSS pixels) and wheel ticks this frame.\n2360:- `pointer?: [number, number, number, number]`: Pointer position (normalised device coordinates), over the canvas (1/0), buttons (`mouseButtons`: what `held` says).\n2361:- `gamepad?: boolean`: Whether a gamepad is connected (`gamepadConnected`), when that changes.\n2362:- `touch?: boolean`: Whether the pointer is a touch (`pointer.touch`), when that changes.\n2363:- `clicks?: [string, 0 | 1, number, number][]`: Pointer buttons pressed (1) and let go (0) this frame, in order, each where the pointer was (`buttonEvents`).\n2369:What input a later frame still reads, as data (`engine.snapshot()`): keys held, presses not yet used and how old they are, the pointer.\n2373:- `readonly pointer: readonly [number, number, number, number]`\n2374:- `readonly gamepad: boolean`\n2429:Camera: drag on the game to orbit/look, pinch to zoom (handled by Input.attachPointer).\n2469:first key / pointer / touch input. Before that, and wherever Web Audio does not exist\n2609:- `vibrato?: { depth: number; rate: number }`: Vibrato depth in semitones and rate in Hz.\n4617:- `readonly view?: Viewport`: The viewport it was recorded on, as it was when the level began (CSS pixels and DPR): the art resolution, pointer aim and the HUD's layout follow it. A headless replay frames for it; a page warns when its own differs. A page resized during the level is not fo…","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GWHRREAFHEkRd2odt3PFZH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj93WWGLrVYWM7o3qNSj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BDS7vGzBPkekkML53yP12y","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211914__x044929/work/_research/engine/pixel-engine/types/engine/input.d.ts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13854,"cache_read_input_tokens":78912,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13854},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"5afa3ea4-8d65-4cb0-93c5-e7fd145389ce","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:24.711Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj93WHNG8GmArQ1DEePo","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BDS7vGzBPkekkML53yP12y":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211914__x044929/work/_research/engine/pixel-engine/types/engine/input.d.ts"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BDS7vGzBPkekkML53yP12y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/**\n2\t * Standard-mapping gamepad buttons → the key codes they press (see character/controls.ts\n3\t * KEYMAP). Change `input.gamepadButtons` to remap. Indices follow the W3C \"standard\" layout:\n4\t * 0 A · 1 B · 2 X · 3 Y · 4 LB · 5 RB · 6 LT · 7 RT · 8 Back · 9 Start · 12–15 d-pad.\n5\t */\n6\texport declare const GAMEPAD_BUTTONS: Readonly<Record<number, string>>;\n7\t/** The parts of the Gamepad API that Input reads (tests can pass plain objects). */\n8\texport interface GamepadLike {\n9\t    readonly connected?: boolean;\n10\t    readonly mapping?: string;\n11\t    readonly axes: readonly number[];\n12\t    readonly buttons: readonly {\n13\t        readonly pressed: boolean;\n14\t        readonly value?: number;\n15\t    }[];\n16\t}\n17\t/**\n18\t * Radial deadzone with rescaling: inside `deadzone` reads 0, the rim reads 1, and the\n19\t * direction is kept (no square-gate snapping to the axes).\n20\t */\n21\texport declare function applyDeadzone(x: number, y: number, deadzone?: number): {\n22\t    x: number;\n23\t    y: number;\n24\t};\n25\t/** How long a queued press stays consumable, in seconds of game time. */\n26\texport declare const PRESS_WINDOW = 0.15;\n27\t/**\n28\t * What the game could read from input in one frame (a recorded frame, see src/engine/replay.ts).\n29\t * Optional fields are left out when empty or zero; `held` and `pointer` also when unchanged\n30\t * from the frame before.\n31\t */\n32\texport interface InputFrame {\n33\t    /** Real seconds this frame lasted (game time follows from it). */\n34\t    dt: number;\n35\t    /** Keys held, keyboard and gamepad buttons together, sorted. */\n36\t    held?: string[];\n37\t    /** Keys pressed since the frame before (a tap can be pressed and not held). */\n38\t    pressed?: string[];\n39\t    /** The touch joystick and the gamepad's left stick (after its deadzone). */\n40\t    analog?: [number, number];\n41\t    pad?: [number, number];\n42\t    /** Pointer movement (CSS pixels) and wheel ticks this frame. */\n43\t    delta?: [number, number];\n44\t    wheel?: number;\n45\t    /** Pointer position (normalised device coordinates), over the canvas (1/0), buttons (`mouseButtons`: what `held` says). */\n46\t    pointer?: [number, number, number, number];\n47\t    /** Whether a gamepad is connected (`gamepadConnected`), when that changes. */\n48\t    gamepad?: boolean;\n49\t    /** Whether the pointer is a touch (`pointer.touch`), when that changes. */\n50\t    touch?: boolean;\n51\t    /** Pointer buttons pressed (1) and let go (0) this frame, in order, each where the pointer was (`buttonEvents`). */\n52\t    clicks?: [string, 0 | 1, number, number][];\n53\t    /** Data from outside the canvas delivered this frame (`send()`): a DOM widget's value, a save read from storage. */\n54\t    commands?: unknown[];\n55\t    /**\n56\t     * Ran in the same task as the frame before (frames of one `step(n)` call): no promise\n57\t     * callbacks ran between them. A replay waits for them before every other frame.\n58\t     */\n59\t    sync?: true;\n60\t}\n61\t/** What input a later frame still reads, as data (`engine.snapshot()`): keys held, presses not yet used and how old they are, the pointer. */\n62\texport interface InputState {\n63\t    readonly held: readonly string[];\n64\t    /** Queued presses: [key, seconds of game time since it was pressed]. */\n65\t    readonly queued: readonly (readonly [string, number])[];\n66\t    readonly pointer: readonly [number, number, number, number];\n67\t    readonly gamepad: boolean;\n68\t    /** Data sent (`send`) and not yet delivered: the next frame that runs delivers it. */\n69\t    readonly outbox: readonly unknown[];\n70\t}\n71\t/** What the frame before held, for `snapshot()` to leave out what did not change. */\n72\texport interface SnapshotMemory {\n73\t    held: string;\n74\t    pointer: string;\n75\t    gamepad?: boolean;\n76\t    touch?: boolean;\n77\t}\n78\t/**\n79\t * Mouse buttons as key codes (`isDown('MouseLeft')`, `consumePress('MouseRight')`), each with\n80\t * its `PointerEvent.buttons` bit, by `PointerEvent.button` (0 left, 1 middle, 2 right).\n81\t */\n82\texport declare const MOUSE_BUTTONS: readonly (readonly [code: string, bit: number])[];\n83\t/** A finger on the canvas, as a key: held while one is down (not a mouse button, so a tap is not a click). */\n84\texport declare const TOUCH_KEY = \"Touch\";\n85\t/** A pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates). */\n86\texport interface ButtonEvent {\n87\t    readonly code: string;\n88\t    readonly down: boolean;\n89\t    readonly x: number;\n90\t    readonly y: number;\n91\t}\n92\t/**\n93\t * Keyboard + pointer + gamepad input.\n94\t * - Keys: held state, per-frame presses (`wasPressed`) and queued presses for fixed-step\n95\t *   code (`consumePress`). Queued presses expire after `pressWindow` s of game time.\n96\t * - Gamepads (standard mapping): the left stick feeds `moveAxis()` (radial deadzone), the\n97\t *   right stick feeds the pointer delta (camera look), buttons press key codes\n98\t *   (`gamepadButtons`). Polled once per frame by the engine (`beginFrame`).\n99\t * - Pointer: accumulated movement per frame (while a button is held or the pointer is\n100\t *   locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\n101\t *   the canvas are keys too (`MOUSE_BUTTONS`: `MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`, `MouseMiddle`), and a\n102\t *   finger is `Touch` (`TOUCH_KEY`), held and pressed like any other, so a click shorter than\n103\t *   a frame is not lost.\n104\t * - Commands (`send`): data from outside the canvas, delivered to the game at the next frame\n105\t *   and recorded with it.\n106\t * - `dispose()` removes every listener it added.\n107\t */\n108\texport declare class Input {\n109\t    private readonly target;\n110\t    private readonly held;\n111\t    private readonly pressed;\n112\t    /** Queued presses → the game time they happened at. */\n113\t    private readonly queued;\n114\t    /** Keys held through gamepad buttons (merged into isDown). */\n115\t    private readonly padHeld;\n116\t    private readonly listeners;\n117\t    /** Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock). */\n118\t    readonly mouseDelta: {\n119\t        x: number;\n120\t        y: number;\n121\t    };\n122\t    /**\n123\t     * Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up:\n124\t     * `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now.\n125\t     * Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\n126\t     */\n127\t    readonly pointer: {\n128\t        x: number;\n129\t        y: number;\n130\t        over: boolean;\n131\t        touch: boolean;\n132\t    };\n133\t    /** Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out). */\n134\t    wheel: number;\n135\t    /** This frame's button presses and releases, in order (`buttonEvents`). */\n136\t    private _buttonEvents;\n137\t    /** Commands sent since the last frame began, and this frame's (`send`, `commands`). */\n138\t    private outbox;\n139\t    private _commands;\n140\t    private lockTarget;\n141\t    /** When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera). */\n142\t    wantsPointerLock: boolean;\n143\t    /** Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active. */\n144\t    readonly analog: {\n145\t        x: number;\n146\t        y: number;\n147\t    };\n148\t    /** Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward). */\n149\t    readonly padAxis: {\n150\t        x: number;\n151\t        y: number;\n152\t    };\n153\t    /** True while any gamepad is connected. */\n154\t    gamepadConnected: boolean;\n155\t    /**\n156\t     * Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's\n157\t     * own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\n158\t     */\n159\t    readonly preventKeys: Set<string>;\n160\t    /** Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS). */\n161\t    gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>;\n162\t    /** Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1). */\n163\t    gamepadDeadzone: number;\n164\t    /** Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt. */\n165\t    gamepadLookSpeed: number;\n166\t    /** Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`. */\n167\t    now: number;\n168\t    /**\n169\t     * True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events,\n170\t     * `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send`\n171\t     * are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\n172\t     */\n173\t    get playing(): boolean;\n174\t    set playing(on: boolean);\n175\t    private _playing;\n176\t    private playedPad;\n177\t    /** Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped. */\n178\t    pressWindow: number;\n179\t    /** `target`: where keys are heard (the page's window); null listens to nothing (`Engine.headless`: input comes from `setKey`, `send`, a replay). */\n180\t    constructor(target?: Window | null);\n181\t    /**\n182\t     * Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the\n183\t     * canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches\n184\t     * pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\n185\t     */\n186\t    attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void;\n187\t    /** Remove every listener this Input added (window and canvas). */\n188\t    dispose(): void;\n189\t    /** Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay. */\n190\t    release(): void;\n191\t    /** Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads). */\n192\t    reset(): void;\n193\t    /**\n194\t     * Engine: begin a frame at game time `now` (seconds). Polls gamepads and drops expired\n195\t     * queued presses. `pads` defaults to `navigator.getGamepads()`; tests can pass fakes.\n196\t     */\n197\t    beginFrame(now: number, dt: number, pads?: readonly (GamepadLike | null)[]): void;\n198\t    get pointerLocked(): boolean;\n199\t    isDown(...codes: string[]): boolean;\n200\t    /** `isDown` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array (fixed-step code). */\n201\t    anyDown(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\n202\t    /** True once per physical key press (valid for the current render frame). */\n203\t    wasPressed(...codes: string[]): boolean;\n204\t    /**\n205\t     * True once per physical key press, kept until consumed or until it is older than\n206\t     * `pressWindow` (150 ms of game time). Use from fixed-step code (which may run zero or\n207\t     * several times per frame) so no press is dropped, while a stale press (made during a\n208\t     * pause, a loading screen or a long hitch) never fires late.\n209\t     */\n210\t    consumePress(...codes: string[]): boolean;\n211\t    /** `consumePress` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array. */\n212\t    consumeAny(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\n213\t    /** Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames. */\n214\t    state(): InputState;\n215\t    /** Back to `state()` at game time `now` (a restore): held keys are those the snapshot held, live ones let go. */\n216\t    setState(s: InputState, now: number): void;\n217\t    /** Presses waiting to be consumed (tooling / tests). */\n218\t    get queuedPresses(): string[];\n219\t    /** Drop queued presses (e.g. when a menu or mode swallows input). */\n220\t    clearQueued(...codes: string[]): void;\n221\t    /**\n222\t     * -1..1 on each axis (x = right, y = forward): the touch joystick or a gamepad's left\n223\t     * stick (whichever is tilted further), else WASD / arrow keys / d-pad.\n224\t     */\n225\t    moveAxis(): {\n226\t        x: number;\n227\t        y: number;\n228\t    };\n229\t    /** Call at the end of each rendered frame. */\n230\t    endFrame(): void;\n231\t    /** Test hook: simulate a key being held (true) or released (false). */\n232\t    setKey(code: string, down: boolean): void;\n233\t    /** Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not. */\n234\t    setPointer(x: number, y: number, down?: boolean): void;\n235\t    /** Test hook: hold mouse buttons (`PointerEvent.buttons` bits: 1 left, 2 right, 4 middle) as the canvas would. */\n236\t    setButtons(bits: number): void;\n237\t    /** Buttons held, as `PointerEvent.buttons` bits (1 left, 2 right, 4 middle; a finger is left): the same keys as `isDown('MouseLeft')`. */\n238\t    get mouseButtons(): number;\n239\t    /** A pointer button (a key code) goes down (pressed, unless held already) or up, where the pointer is. */\n240\t    private button;\n241\t    /**\n242\t     * This frame's pointer button presses and releases, in order, each with where the pointer\n243\t     * was: a drag shorter than a frame (a script's) still starts where it started and ends where\n244\t     * it ended. Recorded with the frame. UI that acts on clicks reads these; play reads `isDown`.\n245\t     */\n246\t    get buttonEvents(): readonly ButtonEvent[];\n247\t    /**\n248\t     * Hand the game data from outside the canvas: a DOM widget's value, a file the player picked,\n249\t     * a save read from storage, anything a game would otherwise take straight from the page. It\n250\t     * arrives in `commands` at the next frame the game runs, and the recording keeps it there, so\n251\t     * a replay delivers the same data at the same frame (and ignores what is sent live). It goes\n252\t     * through JSON first: live play reads exactly what a replay will.\n253\t     */\n254\t    send(command: unknown): void;\n255\t    /**\n256\t     * This frame's commands (`send`), oldest first; empty on most frames. They last one rendered\n257\t     * frame: read them in `update` (`fixedUpdate` runs zero or more times a frame).\n258\t     */\n259\t    get commands(): readonly unknown[];\n260\t    /** Engine: a live frame begins to run: what was sent since the last one becomes its `commands`. */\n261\t    deliver(): void;\n262\t    /** Test hook: inject pointer movement / wheel for the next frame. */\n263\t    addPointer(dx: number, dy: number, wheel?: number): void;\n264\t    /**\n265\t     * This frame's input as data (after `beginFrame`), for a recording. `last` is the frame\n266\t     * before: unchanged held keys, pointer and gamepad connection are left out.\n267\t     */\n268\t    snapshot(dt: number, last?: SnapshotMemory): InputFrame;\n269\t    /**\n270\t     * Replay, before the engine's `beginFrame`: the frame's held keys and presses (presses queue\n271\t     * at the time they would have arrived, the frame before's game time).\n272\t     */\n273\t    playBefore(f: InputFrame): void;\n274\t    /** Replay, after `beginFrame` (which polled no gamepads): sticks, pointer, wheel, gamepad connection. */\n275\t    playAfter(f: InputFrame): void;\n276\t    private press;\n277\t    private pollGamepads;\n278\t}\n279\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"bcbeff92-f14f-40f0-81de-49cfb8eec7ef","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:24.721Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211914__x044929/work/_research/engine/pixel-engine/types/engine/input.d.ts","content":"/**\n * Standard-mapping gamepad buttons → the key codes they press (see character/controls.ts\n * KEYMAP). Change `input.gamepadButtons` to remap. Indices follow the W3C \"standard\" layout:\n * 0 A · 1 B · 2 X · 3 Y · 4 LB · 5 RB · 6 LT · 7 RT · 8 Back · 9 Start · 12–15 d-pad.\n */\nexport declare const GAMEPAD_BUTTONS: Readonly<Record<number, string>>;\n/** The parts of the Gamepad API that Input reads (tests can pass plain objects). */\nexport interface GamepadLike {\n    readonly connected?: boolean;\n    readonly mapping?: string;\n    readonly axes: readonly number[];\n    readonly buttons: readonly {\n        readonly pressed: boolean;\n        readonly value?: number;\n    }[];\n}\n/**\n * Radial deadzone with rescaling: inside `deadzone` reads 0, the rim reads 1, and the\n * direction is kept (no square-gate snapping to the axes).\n */\nexport declare function applyDeadzone(x: number, y: number, deadzone?: number): {\n    x: number;\n    y: number;\n};\n/** How long a queued press stays consumable, in seconds of game time. */\nexport declare const PRESS_WINDOW = 0.15;\n/**\n * What the game could read from input in one frame (a recorded frame, see src/engine/replay.ts).\n * Optional fields are left out when empty or zero; `held` and `pointer` also when unchanged\n * from the frame before.\n */\nexport interface InputFrame {\n    /** Real seconds this frame lasted (game time follows from it). */\n    dt: number;\n    /** Keys held, keyboard and gamepad buttons together, sorted. */\n    held?: string[];\n    /** Keys pressed since the frame before (a tap can be pressed and not held). */\n    pressed?: string[];\n    /** The touch joystick and the gamepad's left stick (after its deadzone). */\n    analog?: [number, number];\n    pad?: [number, number];\n    /** Pointer movement (CSS pixels) and wheel ticks this frame. */\n    delta?: [number, number];\n    wheel?: number;\n    /** Pointer position (normalised device coordinates), over the canvas (1/0), buttons (`mouseButtons`: what `held` says). */\n    pointer?: [number, number, number, number];\n    /** Whether a gamepad is connected (`gamepadConnected`), when that changes. */\n    gamepad?: boolean;\n    /** Whether the pointer is a touch (`pointer.touch`), when that changes. */\n    touch?: boolean;\n    /** Pointer buttons pressed (1) and let go (0) this frame, in order, each where the pointer was (`buttonEvents`). */\n    clicks?: [string, 0 | 1, number, number][];\n    /** Data from outside the canvas delivered this frame (`send()`): a DOM widget's value, a save read from storage. */\n    commands?: unknown[];\n    /**\n     * Ran in the same task as the frame before (frames of one `step(n)` call): no promise\n     * callbacks ran between them. A replay waits for them before every other frame.\n     */\n    sync?: true;\n}\n/** What input a later frame still reads, as data (`engine.snapshot()`): keys held, presses not yet used and how old they are, the pointer. */\nexport interface InputState {\n    readonly held: readonly string[];\n    /** Queued presses: [key, seconds of game time since it was pressed]. */\n    readonly queued: readonly (readonly [string, number])[];\n    readonly pointer: readonly [number, number, number, number];\n    readonly gamepad: boolean;\n    /** Data sent (`send`) and not yet delivered: the next frame that runs delivers it. */\n    readonly outbox: readonly unknown[];\n}\n/** What the frame before held, for `snapshot()` to leave out what did not change. */\nexport interface SnapshotMemory {\n    held: string;\n    pointer: string;\n    gamepad?: boolean;\n    touch?: boolean;\n}\n/**\n * Mouse buttons as key codes (`isDown('MouseLeft')`, `consumePress('MouseRight')`), each with\n * its `PointerEvent.buttons` bit, by `PointerEvent.button` (0 left, 1 middle, 2 right).\n */\nexport declare const MOUSE_BUTTONS: readonly (readonly [code: string, bit: number])[];\n/** A finger on the canvas, as a key: held while one is down (not a mouse button, so a tap is not a click). */\nexport declare const TOUCH_KEY = \"Touch\";\n/** A pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates). */\nexport interface ButtonEvent {\n    readonly code: string;\n    readonly down: boolean;\n    readonly x: number;\n    readonly y: number;\n}\n/**\n * Keyboard + pointer + gamepad input.\n * - Keys: held state, per-frame presses (`wasPressed`) and queued presses for fixed-step\n *   code (`consumePress`). Queued presses expire after `pressWindow` s of game time.\n * - Gamepads (standard mapping): the left stick feeds `moveAxis()` (radial deadzone), the\n *   right stick feeds the pointer delta (camera look), buttons press key codes\n *   (`gamepadButtons`). Polled once per frame by the engine (`beginFrame`).\n * - Pointer: accumulated movement per frame (while a button is held or the pointer is\n *   locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\n *   the canvas are keys too (`MOUSE_BUTTONS`: `MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`, `MouseMiddle`), and a\n *   finger is `Touch` (`TOUCH_KEY`), held and pressed like any other, so a click shorter than\n *   a frame is not lost.\n * - Commands (`send`): data from outside the canvas, delivered to the game at the next frame\n *   and recorded with it.\n * - `dispose()` removes every listener it added.\n */\nexport declare class Input {\n    private readonly target;\n    private readonly held;\n    private readonly pressed;\n    /** Queued presses → the game time they happened at. */\n    private readonly queued;\n    /** Keys held through gamepad buttons (merged into isDown). */\n    private readonly padHeld;\n    private readonly listeners;\n    /** Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock). */\n    readonly mouseDelta: {\n        x: number;\n        y: number;\n    };\n    /**\n     * Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up:\n     * `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now.\n     * Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\n     */\n    readonly pointer: {\n        x: number;\n        y: number;\n        over: boolean;\n        touch: boolean;\n    };\n    /** Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out). */\n    wheel: number;\n    /** This frame's button presses and releases, in order (`buttonEvents`). */\n    private _buttonEvents;\n    /** Commands sent since the last frame began, and this frame's (`send`, `commands`). */\n    private outbox;\n    private _commands;\n    private lockTarget;\n    /** When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera). */\n    wantsPointerLock: boolean;\n    /** Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active. */\n    readonly analog: {\n        x: number;\n        y: number;\n    };\n    /** Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward). */\n    readonly padAxis: {\n        x: number;\n        y: number;\n    };\n    /** True while any gamepad is connected. */\n    gamepadConnected: boolean;\n    /**\n     * Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's\n     * own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\n     */\n    readonly preventKeys: Set<string>;\n    /** Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS). */\n    gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>;\n    /** Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1). */\n    gamepadDeadzone: number;\n    /** Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt. */\n    gamepadLookSpeed: number;\n    /** Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`. */\n    now: number;\n    /**\n     * True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events,\n     * `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send`\n     * are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\n     */\n    get playing(): boolean;\n    set playing(on: boolean);\n    private _playing;\n    private playedPad;\n    /** Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped. */\n    pressWindow: number;\n    /** `target`: where keys are heard (the page's window); null listens to nothing (`Engine.headless`: input comes from `setKey`, `send`, a replay). */\n    constructor(target?: Window | null);\n    /**\n     * Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the\n     * canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches\n     * pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\n     */\n    attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void;\n    /** Remove every listener this Input added (window and canvas). */\n    dispose(): void;\n    /** Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay. */\n    release(): void;\n    /** Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads). */\n    reset(): void;\n    /**\n     * Engine: begin a frame at game time `now` (seconds). Polls gamepads and drops expired\n     * queued presses. `pads` defaults to `navigator.getGamepads()`; tests can pass fakes.\n     */\n    beginFrame(now: number, dt: number, pads?: readonly (GamepadLike | null)[]): void;\n    get pointerLocked(): boolean;\n    isDown(...codes: string[]): boolean;\n    /** `isDown` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array (fixed-step code). */\n    anyDown(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\n    /** True once per physical key press (valid for the current render frame). */\n    wasPressed(...codes: string[]): boolean;\n    /**\n     * True once per physical key press, kept until consumed or until it is older than\n     * `pressWindow` (150 ms of game time). Use from fixed-step code (which may run zero or\n     * several times per frame) so no press is dropped, while a stale press (made during a\n     * pause, a loading screen or a long hitch) never fires late.\n     */\n    consumePress(...codes: string[]): boolean;\n    /** `consumePress` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array. */\n    consumeAny(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\n    /** Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames. */\n    state(): InputState;\n    /** Back to `state()` at game time `now` (a restore): held keys are those the snapshot held, live ones let go. */\n    setState(s: InputState, now: number): void;\n    /** Presses waiting to be consumed (tooling / tests). */\n    get queuedPresses(): string[];\n    /** Drop queued presses (e.g. when a menu or mode swallows input). */\n    clearQueued(...codes: string[]): void;\n    /**\n     * -1..1 on each axis (x = right, y = forward): the touch joystick or a gamepad's left\n     * stick (whichever is tilted further), else WASD / arrow keys / d-pad.\n     */\n    moveAxis(): {\n        x: number;\n        y: number;\n    };\n    /** Call at the end of each rendered frame. */\n    endFrame(): void;\n    /** Test hook: simulate a key being held (true) or released (false). */\n    setKey(code: string, down: boolean): void;\n    /** Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not. */\n    setPointer(x: number, y: number, down?: boolean): void;\n    /** Test hook: hold mouse buttons (`PointerEvent.buttons` bits: 1 left, 2 right, 4 middle) as the canvas would. */\n    setButtons(bits: number): void;\n    /** Buttons held, as `PointerEvent.buttons` bits (1 left, 2 right, 4 middle; a finger is left): the same keys as `isDown('MouseLeft')`. */\n    get mouseButtons(): number;\n    /** A pointer button (a key code) goes down (pressed, unless held already) or up, where the pointer is. */\n    private button;\n    /**\n     * This frame's pointer button presses and releases, in order, each with where the pointer\n     * was: a drag shorter than a frame (a script's) still starts where it started and ends where\n     * it ended. Recorded with the frame. UI that acts on clicks reads these; play reads `isDown`.\n     */\n    get buttonEvents(): readonly ButtonEvent[];\n    /**\n     * Hand the game data from outside the canvas: a DOM widget's value, a file the player picked,\n     * a save read from storage, anything a game would otherwise take straight from the page. It\n     * arrives in `commands` at the next frame the game runs, and the recording keeps it there, so\n     * a replay delivers the same data at the same frame (and ignores what is sent live). It goes\n     * through JSON first: live play reads exactly what a replay will.\n     */\n    send(command: unknown): void;\n    /**\n     * This frame's commands (`send`), oldest first; empty on most frames. They last one rendered\n     * frame: read them in `update` (`fixedUpdate` runs zero or more times a frame).\n     */\n    get commands(): readonly unknown[];\n    /** Engine: a live frame begins to run: what was sent since the last one becomes its `commands`. */\n    deliver(): void;\n    /** Test hook: inject pointer movement / wheel for the next frame. */\n    addPointer(dx: number, dy: number, wheel?: number): void;\n    /**\n     * This frame's input as data (after `beginFrame`), for a recording. `last` is the frame\n     * before: unchanged held keys, pointer and gamepad connection are left out.\n     */\n    snapshot(dt: number, last?: SnapshotMemory): InputFrame;\n    /**\n     * Replay, before the engine's `beginFrame`: the frame's held keys and presses (presses queue\n     * at the time they would have arrived, the frame before's game time).\n     */\n    playBefore(f: InputFrame): void;\n    /** Replay, after `beginFrame` (which polled no gamepads): sticks, pointer, wheel, gamepad connection. */\n    playAfter(f: InputFrame): void;\n    private press;\n    private pollGamepads;\n}\n","numLines":279,"startLine":1,"totalLines":279}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BDS7vGzBPkekkML53yP12y","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj93WWGLrVYWM7o3qNSj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015PFhJ5SGkxtqQfX2FsQKpK","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211914__x044929/work/_research/engine/pixel-engine/types/engine/hud/Hud.d.ts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13854,"cache_read_input_tokens":78912,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13854},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"8639ddbf-ed2d-4082-b274-3f45b4f3d0e9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:26.031Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj93WHNG8GmArQ1DEePo","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015PFhJ5SGkxtqQfX2FsQKpK":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211914__x044929/work/_research/engine/pixel-engine/types/engine/hud/Hud.d.ts"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015PFhJ5SGkxtqQfX2FsQKpK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport type { Framing, Resolution } from '../framing';\n2\timport { type PaletteColor } from '../palette';\n3\t/** Where an element is attached on screen; it is also aligned that way (right-anchored text grows left). */\n4\texport type HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right';\n5\texport type HudColor = PaletteColor | number;\n6\texport interface HudOptions {\n7\t    /** Default 'white'. */\n8\t    color?: HudColor;\n9\t    /** 1-pixel drop shadow color, or false. Default 'ink'. */\n10\t    shadow?: HudColor | false;\n11\t    /** Integer art-pixel scale (2 = double-size glyphs). Default 1. */\n12\t    scale?: number;\n13\t    /** Default 'top-left': x/y are offsets from that screen corner/edge, in art pixels. */\n14\t    anchor?: HudAnchor;\n15\t}\n16\t/**\n17\t * Pixel HUD: crisp text and icons drawn in art pixels on top of the game, never through\n18\t * the post filters. It is a 2D canvas at the internal resolution (480×270 / 320×180),\n19\t * laid over the game canvas with the same integer scale and letterbox offset\n20\t * (`framing.ts`), so one HUD pixel is exactly one art pixel at every resolution.\n21\t *\n22\t * Retained: what you add stays on screen until `clear()`. Redraw everything each frame\n23\t * (clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\n24\t * resolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\n25\t *\n26\t *   ctx.hud.clear();\n27\t *   ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\n28\t *   ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\n29\t */\n30\texport declare class Hud {\n31\t    private readonly container;\n32\t    /** The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn). */\n33\t    canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null;\n34\t    visible: boolean;\n35\t    private items;\n36\t    private drawn;\n37\t    private size;\n38\t    private layoutKey;\n39\t    constructor(container: HTMLElement | null);\n40\t    /** HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution). */\n41\t    get width(): number;\n42\t    get height(): number;\n43\t    /** Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation). */\n44\t    text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options?: HudOptions): void;\n45\t    /** A filled rectangle (panels, bars). */\n46\t    rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor?: HudAnchor): void;\n47\t    /**\n48\t     * A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped\n49\t     * through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = transparent).\n50\t     *\n51\t     *   hud.sprite(4, 4, ['.yy.', 'ywyy', 'yyyy', '.yy.'], { y: 'sand', w: 'white' });\n52\t     */\n53\t    sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options?: HudOptions): void;\n54\t    /** Remove everything. */\n55\t    clear(): void;\n56\t    /** Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`. */\n57\t    measure(text: string, scale?: number): {\n58\t        width: number;\n59\t        height: number;\n60\t    };\n61\t    /** Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed. */\n62\t    sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void;\n63\t    dispose(): void;\n64\t    private createCanvas;\n65\t    private paint;\n66\t    private glyphs;\n67\t    private place;\n68\t}\n69\t/**\n70\t * Top-left corner, in whole art pixels, of a w×h element placed at offset (x, y) from\n71\t * `anchor` on a screen of `size` art pixels. Pure (unit-tested).\n72\t */\n73\texport declare function hudPlace(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, anchor: HudAnchor, size: Resolution): [number, number];\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"f8f9ccee-5a31-42e7-bf32-293a06bf5a29","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:26.040Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211914__x044929/work/_research/engine/pixel-engine/types/engine/hud/Hud.d.ts","content":"import type { Framing, Resolution } from '../framing';\nimport { type PaletteColor } from '../palette';\n/** Where an element is attached on screen; it is also aligned that way (right-anchored text grows left). */\nexport type HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right';\nexport type HudColor = PaletteColor | number;\nexport interface HudOptions {\n    /** Default 'white'. */\n    color?: HudColor;\n    /** 1-pixel drop shadow color, or false. Default 'ink'. */\n    shadow?: HudColor | false;\n    /** Integer art-pixel scale (2 = double-size glyphs). Default 1. */\n    scale?: number;\n    /** Default 'top-left': x/y are offsets from that screen corner/edge, in art pixels. */\n    anchor?: HudAnchor;\n}\n/**\n * Pixel HUD: crisp text and icons drawn in art pixels on top of the game, never through\n * the post filters. It is a 2D canvas at the internal resolution (480×270 / 320×180),\n * laid over the game canvas with the same integer scale and letterbox offset\n * (`framing.ts`), so one HUD pixel is exactly one art pixel at every resolution.\n *\n * Retained: what you add stays on screen until `clear()`. Redraw everything each frame\n * (clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\n * resolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\n *\n *   ctx.hud.clear();\n *   ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\n *   ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\n */\nexport declare class Hud {\n    private readonly container;\n    /** The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn). */\n    canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null;\n    visible: boolean;\n    private items;\n    private drawn;\n    private size;\n    private layoutKey;\n    constructor(container: HTMLElement | null);\n    /** HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution). */\n    get width(): number;\n    get height(): number;\n    /** Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation). */\n    text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options?: HudOptions): void;\n    /** A filled rectangle (panels, bars). */\n    rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor?: HudAnchor): void;\n    /**\n     * A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped\n     * through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = transparent).\n     *\n     *   hud.sprite(4, 4, ['.yy.', 'ywyy', 'yyyy', '.yy.'], { y: 'sand', w: 'white' });\n     */\n    sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options?: HudOptions): void;\n    /** Remove everything. */\n    clear(): void;\n    /** Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`. */\n    measure(text: string, scale?: number): {\n        width: number;\n        height: number;\n    };\n    /** Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed. */\n    sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void;\n    dispose(): void;\n    private createCanvas;\n    private paint;\n    private glyphs;\n    private place;\n}\n/**\n * Top-left corner, in whole art pixels, of a w×h element placed at offset (x, y) from\n * `anchor` on a screen of `size` art pixels. Pure (unit-tested).\n */\nexport declare function hudPlace(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, anchor: HudAnchor, size: Resolution): [number, number];\n","numLines":74,"startLine":1,"totalLines":74}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015PFhJ5SGkxtqQfX2FsQKpK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
