{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M3v9YM7Rv4YFHbZb4pPzRh","type":"tool_result","content":"## 7. Input and touch\n\n### applyDeadzone()\n\n```ts\nfunction applyDeadzone(x: number, y: number, deadzone = 0.2): { x: number; y: number }\n```\n\nRadial deadzone with rescaling: inside `deadzone` reads 0, the rim reads 1, and the\ndirection is kept (no square-gate snapping to the axes).\n\n### interface ButtonEvent\n\nA pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates).\n\n- `readonly code: string`\n- `readonly down: boolean`\n- `readonly x: number`\n- `readonly y: number`\n\n### DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS\n\n```ts\nconst DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS: readonly TouchButton[]\n```\n\nDefault buttons for PlatformerCharacter (see character/controls.ts KEYMAP).\n\n### GAMEPAD_BUTTONS\n\n```ts\nconst GAMEPAD_BUTTONS: Readonly<Record<number, string>>\n```\n\nStandard-mapping gamepad buttons → the key codes they press (see character/controls.ts\nKEYMAP). Change `input.gamepadButtons` to remap. Indices follow the W3C \"standard\" layout:\n0 A · 1 B · 2 X · 3 Y · 4 LB · 5 RB · 6 LT · 7 RT · 8 Back · 9 Start · 12–15 d-pad.\n\n### interface GamepadLike\n\nThe parts of the Gamepad API that Input reads (tests can pass plain objects).\n\n- `readonly connected?: boolean`\n- `readonly mapping?: string`\n- `readonly axes: readonly number[]`\n- `readonly buttons: readonly { readonly pressed: boolean; readonly value?: number }[]`\n\n### class Input\n\nKeyboard + pointer + gamepad input.\n....\n12:6. Characters: `JumpKind`, `KEYMAP`, `MoveInput`, `MoveState`, `PlatformerCharacter`, `PlatformerOptions`, `readMoveInput`\n13:7. Input and touch: `applyDeadzone`, `ButtonEvent`, `DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS`, `GAMEPAD_BUTTONS`, `GamepadLike`, `Input`, `InputFrame`, `InputState`, `MOUSE_BUTTONS`, `PRESS_WINDOW`, `TOUCH_KEY`, `TouchButton`, `TouchButtonState`, `TouchControls`, `TouchCorner`\n14-8. Audio: `attenuation`, `AudioManager`, `AudioSettings`, `Instrument`, `Listener`, `muffleCutoff`, `noteFrequency`, `parseSong`, `PLAYGROUND_SONG`, `PlayOptions`, `renderSound`, `SFX`, `SfxName`, `Song`, `SoundDef`, `Spatial`, `spatialize`, `SpatialOptions`, `Voice`, `VoiceSettings`, `VolumeChannel`, `Wave`\n15-9. Particles: `BurstOptions`, `ParticlePool`, `ParticlePreset`, `ParticlePresetName`, `Particles`, `PARTICLES`\n16-10. HUD: `Hud`, `HudAnchor`, `HudColor`, `HudOptions`, `hudPlace`\n## 6. Characters\n\n### type JumpKind\n\n```ts\ntype JumpKind = 'Jump' | 'JumpUp' | 'DoubleJump' | 'TripleJump' | 'Backflip' | 'SideFlip' | 'LongJump' | 'WallKick' | 'JumpKick'\n```\n\n### KEYMAP\n\n```ts\nconst KEYMAP: { readonly jump: readonly [\"Space\"]; readonly walk: readonly [\"ShiftLeft\", \"ShiftRight\"]; readonly crouch: readonly [\"KeyC\", \"ControlLeft\", \"ControlRight\"]; readonly prone: readonly [\"KeyZ\"]; readonly lie: readonly [\"KeyX\"]; readonly grab: readonly [...]; readonly attack: readonly [...\n```\n\nDefault key map for PlatformerCharacter. Movement is camera-relative for every preset\n(strafing in first person; left/right only on a side-scroller lane, except while\nclimbing or hanging). Call from Game.fixedUpdate.\n\n  WASD / arrows  move          Shift   walk / tiptoe\n2140:### KEYMAP\n2141-\n2142-```ts\n2143-const KEYMAP: { readonly jump: readonly [\"Space\"]; readonly walk: readonly [\"ShiftLeft\", \"ShiftRight\"]; readonly crouch: readonly [\"KeyC\", \"ControlLeft\", \"ControlRight\"]; readonly prone: readonly [\"KeyZ\"]; readonly lie: readonly [\"KeyX\"]; readonly grab: readonly [...]; readonly attack: readonly\n2144-```\n2145-\n2146-Default key map for PlatformerCharacter. Movement is camera-relative for every preset\n2147-(strafing in first person; left/right only on a side-scroller lane, except while\n2148-climbing or hanging). Call from Game.fixedUpdate.\n2149-\n2150-  WASD / arrows  move          Shift   walk / tiptoe\n2151-  Space          jump          C / Ctrl crouch (air: ground pound)\n2152-  Z              prone toggle  X        lie down / get up\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n// check.mjs: play a Pixel Engine game in a real browser and report what happened.\n// Ships in the engine kit; run it before you hand a game back.\n//\n//   node check.mjs                       index.html in the current folder\n//   node check.mjs examples/looks.html   any page (served from the folder that holds pixel-engine.js)\n//   node check.mjs \"index.html?look=noir&camera=side\"   with URL flags\n//   node check.mjs http://localhost:5173/\n//   node check.mjs --sheets models.js    sheets of your own models and textures (no page played)\n//   node check.mjs --headless game.js    play the game in Node, no browser: steps, errors, a replay\n//\n// Options:\n//   --keys KeyD*60,Space*4,KeyW*30   hold each key for that many frames, in order (default: 90 idle frames)\n//   --cameras                        also shoot the iso, topdown, side and third camera presets\n//   --looks pixel_heroes,noir        also shoot these looks (names from engine.lookPresets)\n//   --out check                      folder for the PNGs and report.json (default: ./check)\n//   --size 960x540                   viewport in CSS pixels\n//   --sheets models.js,crate,cobbles draw sheets instead of playing a page (ASSETS.md): every\n//                                    ModelDef and TextureDef a module exports (by name, in an\n//                                    array or object, in a ModelCatalog / TextureCatalog, or added\n//                                    to the library), and library ids. A PNG each and report.json\n//                                    in --out (default ./check/sheets); exit 1 on any problem\n//   --headless [game.js]             play a game module in Node with Engine.headless instead of a\n//                                    page (no browser, no pictures): it imports the module, makes\n//                                    the game its `createGame()` export returns, plays the --keys\n//                                    frames, then replays that run's recording in a fresh game. It\n//                                    writes report.json (state, errors, fingerprint) to --out; exit\n//                                    1 on an error or a replay that ends somewhere else\n//   --help                           this text\n//\n// It needs Node 20.15+ (or 22.2+) and, except for --headless, Playwright (`npm i -D playwright` then\n// `npx playwright install chromium`; a global install, `npm i -g playwright`, works too), or\n// `playwright-core` with CHROMIUM_PATH set to a Chromium (its headless shell,\n// `chrome-linux/headless_shell`, is the lightest): it plays WebGPU on SwiftShader with no\n// display. Exit code 0 means the game started, ran the frames with no errors (page, console,\n// engine or GPU) and drew a picture (with --sheets: every sheet was drawn and no\n// def has a problem; warnings are fine); 1 means it didn't; 2 means the tool couldn't run (bad\n// arguments, no page, no browser, or a browser without WebGPU, which no game can start in).\nimport { execSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { createServer } from 'node:http';\nimport { existsSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, statSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\nimport { basename, dirname, extname, isAbsolute, join, relative, resolve, sep } from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\nimport * as zlib from 'node:zlib';\n\nconst usage = () => readFileSync(new URL(import.meta.url), 'utf8').split('\\nimport ')[0].replace(/^#!.*\\n/, '').replace(/^\\/\\/ ?/gm, '');\nconst fail = (message) => {\n  console.error(`check.mjs: ${message}\\n\\n${usage()}`);\n  process.exit(2);\n};\nif (typeof zlib.crc32 !== 'function') fail(`needs Node 20.15+ or 22.2+ (this is ${process.version})`);\n\n// --name value flags, --name flags, then one positional page\nconst VALUE = new Set(['keys', 'looks', 'out', 'size', 'sheets']);\nconst FLAG = new Set(['cameras', 'help', 'headless']);\nconst opts = {};\nconst positional = [];\nfor (let i = 2; i < process.argv.length; i++) {\n  const a = process.argv[i];","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"532fb96c-ce48-429c-83da-e4dc23da31e0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:22:12.093Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## 7. Input and touch\n\n### applyDeadzone()\n\n```ts\nfunction applyDeadzone(x: number, y: number, deadzone = 0.2): { x: number; y: number }\n```\n\nRadial deadzone with rescaling: inside `deadzone` reads 0, the rim reads 1, and the\ndirection is kept (no square-gate snapping to the axes).\n\n### interface ButtonEvent\n\nA pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates).\n\n- `readonly code: string`\n- `readonly down: boolean`\n- `readonly x: number`\n- `readonly y: number`\n\n### DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS\n\n```ts\nconst DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS: readonly TouchButton[]\n```\n\nDefault buttons for PlatformerCharacter (see character/controls.ts KEYMAP).\n\n### GAMEPAD_BUTTONS\n\n```ts\nconst GAMEPAD_BUTTONS: Readonly<Record<number, string>>\n```\n\nStandard-mapping gamepad buttons → the key codes they press (see character/controls.ts\nKEYMAP). Change `input.gamepadButtons` to remap. Indices follow the W3C \"standard\" layout:\n0 A · 1 B · 2 X · 3 Y · 4 LB · 5 RB · 6 LT · 7 RT · 8 Back · 9 Start · 12–15 d-pad.\n\n### interface GamepadLike\n\nThe parts of the Gamepad API that Input reads (tests can pass plain objects).\n\n- `readonly connected?: boolean`\n- `readonly mapping?: string`\n- `readonly axes: readonly number[]`\n- `readonly buttons: readonly { readonly pressed: boolean; readonly value?: number }[]`\n\n### class Input\n\nKeyboard + pointer + gamepad input.\n....\n12:6. Characters: `JumpKind`, `KEYMAP`, `MoveInput`, `MoveState`, `PlatformerCharacter`, `PlatformerOptions`, `readMoveInput`\n13:7. Input and touch: `applyDeadzone`, `ButtonEvent`, `DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS`, `GAMEPAD_BUTTONS`, `GamepadLike`, `Input`, `InputFrame`, `InputState`, `MOUSE_BUTTONS`, `PRESS_WINDOW`, `TOUCH_KEY`, `TouchButton`, `TouchButtonState`, `TouchControls`, `TouchCorner`\n14-8. Audio: `attenuation`, `AudioManager`, `AudioSettings`, `Instrument`, `Listener`, `muffleCutoff`, `noteFrequency`, `parseSong`, `PLAYGROUND_SONG`, `PlayOptions`, `renderSound`, `SFX`, `SfxName`, `Song`, `SoundDef`, `Spatial`, `spatialize`, `SpatialOptions`, `Voice`, `VoiceSettings`, `VolumeChannel`, `Wave`\n15-9. Particles: `BurstOptions`, `ParticlePool`, `ParticlePreset`, `ParticlePresetName`, `Particles`, `PARTICLES`\n16-10. HUD: `Hud`, `HudAnchor`, `HudColor`, `HudOptions`, `hudPlace`\n## 6. Characters\n\n### type JumpKind\n\n```ts\ntype JumpKind = 'Jump' | 'JumpUp' | 'DoubleJump' | 'TripleJump' | 'Backflip' | 'SideFlip' | 'LongJump' | 'WallKick' | 'JumpKick'\n```\n\n### KEYMAP\n\n```ts\nconst KEYMAP: { readonly jump: readonly [\"Space\"]; readonly walk: readonly [\"ShiftLeft\", \"ShiftRight\"]; readonly crouch: readonly [\"KeyC\", \"ControlLeft\", \"ControlRight\"]; readonly prone: readonly [\"KeyZ\"]; readonly lie: readonly [\"KeyX\"]; readonly grab: readonly [...]; readonly attack: readonly [...\n```\n\nDefault key map for PlatformerCharacter. Movement is camera-relative for every preset\n(strafing in first person; left/right only on a side-scroller lane, except while\nclimbing or hanging). Call from Game.fixedUpdate.\n\n  WASD / arrows  move          Shift   walk / tiptoe\n2140:### KEYMAP\n2141-\n2142-```ts\n2143-const KEYMAP: { readonly jump: readonly [\"Space\"]; readonly walk: readonly [\"ShiftLeft\", \"ShiftRight\"]; readonly crouch: readonly [\"KeyC\", \"ControlLeft\", \"ControlRight\"]; readonly prone: readonly [\"KeyZ\"]; readonly lie: readonly [\"KeyX\"]; readonly grab: readonly [...]; readonly attack: readonly\n2144-```\n2145-\n2146-Default key map for PlatformerCharacter. Movement is camera-relative for every preset\n2147-(strafing in first person; left/right only on a side-scroller lane, except while\n2148-climbing or hanging). Call from Game.fixedUpdate.\n2149-\n2150-  WASD / arrows  move          Shift   walk / tiptoe\n2151-  Space          jump          C / Ctrl crouch (air: ground pound)\n2152-  Z              prone toggle  X        lie down / get up\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n// check.mjs: play a Pixel Engine game in a real browser and report what happened.\n// Ships in the engine kit; run it before you hand a game back.\n//\n//   node check.mjs                       index.html in the current folder\n//   node check.mjs examples/looks.html   any page (served from the folder that holds pixel-engine.js)\n//   node check.mjs \"index.html?look=noir&camera=side\"   with URL flags\n//   node check.mjs http://localhost:5173/\n//   node check.mjs --sheets models.js    sheets of your own models and textures (no page played)\n//   node check.mjs --headless game.js    play the game in Node, no browser: steps, errors, a replay\n//\n// Options:\n//   --keys KeyD*60,Space*4,KeyW*30   hold each key for that many frames, in order (default: 90 idle frames)\n//   --cameras                        also shoot the iso, topdown, side and third camera presets\n//   --looks pixel_heroes,noir        also shoot these looks (names from engine.lookPresets)\n//   --out check                      folder for the PNGs and report.json (default: ./check)\n//   --size 960x540                   viewport in CSS pixels\n//   --sheets models.js,crate,cobbles draw sheets instead of playing a page (ASSETS.md): every\n//                                    ModelDef and TextureDef a module exports (by name, in an\n//                                    array or object, in a ModelCatalog / TextureCatalog, or added\n//                                    to the library), and library ids. A PNG each and report.json\n//                                    in --out (default ./check/