{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011Pf5Vp1yrJgjkEXFb386Nc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t=== class Timeline (line 4881)\n2\t### class Timeline\n3\t\n4\t- `new Timeline(o: TimelineOptions)`\n5\t- `readonly duration: number`\n6\t- `time: number`: The playhead (s).\n7\t- `playing: boolean`\n8\t- `speed: number`: Playback rate (1: real time, 0.5: slow motion).\n9\t- `ended: boolean`: True once the end has been reached (by playing or skipping).\n10\t- `readonly fired: string[]`: Cue names in the order they fired (tests and tools).\n11\t- `play(): void`\n12\t- `pause(): void`\n13\t- `update(dt: number): void`: Advance by `dt` seconds of game time (times `speed`) while playing, firing the cues passed.\n14\t- `seek(t: number): void`: Move the playhead to `t` without firing the cues in between (scrubbing). Cues before `t` count as done and cues after it will fire again (going back re-arms them). Ignored while skipping (a cue that loops back cannot undo a skip).\n15\t- `skip(): void`: Jump to the end: the cues not yet fired run (except the cosmetic ones), then `onEnd`. Cues after `duration` never fire, played or skipped.\n16\t- `camera(t = this.time): CameraShot | null`: Where the camera is at `t` (default now): on each key at its time, gliding between keys on a smooth curve (Catmull-Rom tangents, so the speed has no jolt at a key; the first and last key of each shot ease in and ou\n17\t- `line(t = this.time): Line | null`: The subtitle showing at `t` (default now), or null.\n18\t- `bars(t = this.time): number`: How far the letterbox bars are in (0..1) at `t` (default now): sliding in at the start, out at the end.\n19\t\n20\t### interface TimelineLine\n21\t\n22\t- `at: number`\n23\t- `until: number`\n24\t- `text: string`\n25\t- `who?: string`: Who is speaking (shown before the text).\n26\t\n27\t### interface TimelineOptions\n28\t\n29\t- `shots?: readonly CameraKey[]`\n30\t- `cues?: readonly Cue[]`\n31\t- `lines?: readonly Line[]`\n32\t- `duration?: number`: Length (s); default the last key, cue or line.\n33\t- `bars?: number`: Seconds the letterbox bars take to slide in and out (default 0.6; 0: no bars).\n34\t- `onEnd?: () => void`: Called once when the playhead reaches the end (or the scene is skipped).\n35\t\n36\t### interface TraceRow\n37\t=== interface TimelineOptions (line 4906)\n38\t### interface TimelineOptions\n39\t\n40\t- `shots?: readonly CameraKey[]`\n41\t- `cues?: readonly Cue[]`\n42\t- `lines?: readonly Line[]`\n43\t- `duration?: number`: Length (s); default the last key, cue or line.\n44\t- `bars?: number`: Seconds the letterbox bars take to slide in and out (default 0.6; 0: no bars).\n45\t- `onEnd?: () => void`: Called once when the playhead reaches the end (or the scene is skipped).\n46\t\n47\t### interface TraceRow\n48\t\n49\t- `name: string`\n50\t- `kind: string`\n51\t- `depth: number`\n52\t- `status: Status | null`: This tick's answer, or null if this tick never reached the node.\n53\t\n54\t### class Trail\n55\t\n56\t- `new Trail(o: TrailOptions = {})`\n57\t- `readonly capacity: number`\n58\t- `width: number`\n59\t- `life: number`\n60\t- `readonly head: Color`: Head and tail colours (live: `trail.head.setHex(...)`).\n61\t- `readonly tail: Color`\n62\t- `push(p: Vector3, time: number): void`: The trail's newest point (call every frame while it moves).\n63\t- `reset(): void`: Drop every point.\n64\t- `get length: number`: Points alive now.\n65\t- `update(time: number, camera: Camera): void`: Per frame: forget old points, rebuild the ribbon facing `camera`.\n66\t- `dispose(): void`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance.\n67\t\n68\t### interface TrailOptions\n69\t\n70\t- `points?: number`: Most points kept. Default 24.\n71\t- `width?: number`: Width at the head (m).\n72\t- `life?: number`: Seconds a point lasts. Default 0.35.\n73\t=== class Decals (line 4127)\n74\t### class Decals\n75\t\n76\t- `new Decals(scene: Scene, o: { capacity?: number } = {})`\n77\t