with a spring motor: it rests at `at` (the spring holds its\n234\town weight), sinks under a load (the character presses with its `weight`) and bounces back.\n235\t\n236\t### interface SpringPadOptions\n237\t\n238\t- `size?: Vec3`\n239\t- `stiffness?: number`: Spring stiffness (1/s²: mass-independent). Higher: firmer. Default 40.\n240\t- `damping?: number`\n241\t- `travel?: number`: How far it can sink (m). Default 0.6.\n242\t- `color?: PaletteColor`\n243\t\n244\t### class Trigger\n245\t\n246\tA sensor volume with enter/exit callbacks. It is not a collider in the world: after\n247\tevery fixed step Physics runs an intersection query for it and diffs the result, so a\n248\ttrigger never blocks the character controller, ray casts or camera rays.\n249\tCreate with `physics.trigger(shape, at, options)`.\n250\t\n251\t- `new Trigger(def: TriggerShape, at: readonly [number, number, number] | Vector3, options: TriggerOptions, accept: (c: RAPIER.Collider) => boolean, detach: (t: Trigger) => void)`\n252\t- `readonly position: Vector3`: World position; move it freely (moving platforms, carried zones).\n253\t=== clothGrid (line 1521)\n254\t### clothGrid()\n255\t\n256\t```ts\n257\tfunction clothGrid(o: ClothOptions): VerletBody & { cols: number; rows: number; uv: Float32Array }\n258\t```\n259\t\n260\tA sheet of cloth: a grid of particles with structural, shear and bend edges, two triangles per cell.\n261\t\n262\t### interface ClothOptions\n263\t\n264\t- `width: number`\n265\t- `height: number`\n266\t- `cols: number`: Particles across and down (≥ 2).\n267\t- `rows: number`\n268\t- `origin: readonly [number, number, number]`: The top-left corner. The cloth lies in the plane spanned by `across` and `down`.\n269\t- `across?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Direction along the top edge (unit). Default +X.\n270\t- `down?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Direction from the top edge to the bottom one (unit). Default −Y (hanging); +Z lays it flat.\n271\t- `pin?: 'top' | 'corners' | 'left' | 'none'`: Pinned particles: the whole top edge, its two corners, the left edge (a flag), or none.\n272\t- `shear?: number`: Shear and bend springs (0..1 stiffness). Default 0.8 / 0.3.\n273\t- `bend?: number`\n274\t- `iterations?: number`\n275\t\n276\t### interface Crumble\n277\t\n278\t- `readonly o: CrumbleOptions`\n279\t- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\n280\t- `collider: RAPIER.Collider | null`\n281\t- `state: 'solid' | 'shaking' | 'falling'`: 'solid' → 'shaking' → 'falling' → (regrow) 'solid'.\n282\t- `t: number`\n283\t\n284\t### interface CrumbleOptions\n285\t\n286\t- `at: Vec3`\n287\t- `size: Vec3`\n288\t- `color: PaletteColor`\n289\t=== class SoftMesh (line 4774)\n290\t### class SoftMesh\n291\t\n292\t- `new SoftMesh(body: VerletBody, material: Material, o: { uv?: Float32Array; doubleSided?: boolean } = {})`\n293\t- `readonly body: VerletBody`\n294\t- `sync(): void`: Copy the particles into the mesh (call once per frame after stepping the body).\n295\t\n296\t### class SpriteBatch\n297\t\n298\t- `new SpriteBatch(sheet: SpriteSheet, o: { capacity: number })`\n299\t- `readonly sheet: SpriteSheet`\n300\t- `spawn(at: readonly [number, number, number], o: SpriteOptions = {}): number`: A new sprite (its index), or -1 when full.\n301\t- `set(i: number, o: SpriteOptions & { at?: readonly [number, number, number] }): void`: Move or change sprite `i`.\n302\t- `put(i: number, x: number, y: number, z: number, frame?: number, flip?: boolean): void`: `set` without the options object, for many sprites every frame: position, then frame and mirror.\n303\t- `at(i: number): [number, number, number]`: Where sprite `i` stands.\n304\t- `frameOf(i: number): number`: The frame sprite `i` shows.\n305\t- `dispose(): this`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance\n306\t\n307\t### interface SpriteOptions\n308\t\n309\t- `size?: number`: Height in metres (the width follows the frame's aspect). Default 1.\n310\t- `frame?: number`\n311\t- `flip?: boolean`: Mirror left-right (a sprite facing the other way).\n312\t\n313\t### interface SpriteSheet\n314\t\n315\t- `readonly texture: Texture`: The sheet (nearest-filtered); `drawSheet` makes one from code. Frames run left to right, top to bottom, from the image's top-left; a texture with `flipY` false (a `DataTexture`) holds its rows top line first.\n316\t- `readonly frame: readonly [number, number]`: Frame size in pixels and the frames across and down.\n317\t- `readonly cols: number`\n318\t- `readonly rows: number`\n319\t- `readonly frames: number`\n320\t\n321\t### swayMaterial()\n322\t\n323\t```ts\n324\tfunction swayMaterial(material: Material, wind: WindUniforms, o: SwayOptions): Material\n325\t=== class RopeMesh (line 4675)\n326\t### class RopeMesh\n327\t\n328\t- `new RopeMesh(body: VerletBody, material: Material, thickness = 0.06)`\n329\t- `readonly body: VerletBody`\n330\t- `sync(): void`\n331\t\n332\t### SCREEN_LAYER\n333\t\n334\t```ts\n335\tconst SCREEN_LAYER: 2\n336\t```\n337\t\n338\tThe layer for screens and mirrors: drawn by the main camera, never by a RenderView.\n339\t\n340\t### class ScreenFx\n341\t\n342\t- `cover(kind: TransitionKind = 'fade', o: TransitionOptions = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Cover the picture (progress → 1). Resolves when it stops: `true` when it is fully covered, `false` when another transition (or `set`, `clear`) took over first.\n343\t- `reveal(kind?: TransitionKind, o: TransitionOptions = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Uncover it (progress → 0) with `kind` (default: the one that covered it). Resolves like `cover`.\n344\t- `transition(kind: TransitionKind, between: () => unknown, o: TransitionOptions & { revealCenter?: TransitionOptions['center'] } = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Cover, run `between` (load a level, teleport), then reveal, also when `between` throws (the error is pas\n345\t- `set(kind: TransitionKind | null, progress: number): void`: Jump straight to a progress (0 clear, 1 covered), no animation.\n346\t- `flash(color: ScreenColor = 'white', o: FlashOptions = {}): void`: A full-screen flash that fades out.\n347\t- `shockwave(at: Vector3 | readonly [number, number], o: ShockwaveOptions = {}): void`: A ring that pushes the picture outwards from `at` (oldest ring is replaced when 4 run).\n348\t- `clear(): void`: Stop everything (a clear picture).\n349\t- `state(): ScreenFxState`\n350\t- `update(dt: number, camera: Camera | null): void`: Engine, every rendered frame (real seconds; `camera` projects world centres).\n351\t- `sampleNode(tex: any, scale: any): any`: Sample an art-resolution picture for the device pass, pushed by the shockwaves and blocked up by a mosaic transition, with the rings' bright edge. `tex` is the art target (a texture node); `scale` is device pixels per\n352\t- `colorNode(color: any, scale: any): any`: The transition and the flash over a finished colour (device pass).\n353\t\n354\t### interface ScreenFxState\n355\t\n356\tWhat `state()` reports (tests, tools).\n357\t\n358\t- `transition: TransitionKind | null`\n359\t- `progress: number`: 0 clear … 1 covered.\n360\t- `moving: boolean`: A transition is animating.\n361\t=== ropeLine (line 1928)\n362\t### ropeLine()\n363\t\n364\t```ts\n365\tfunction ropeLine(from: readonly [number, number, number], to: readonly [number, number, number], segments: number, o: { pinEnd?: boolean; slack?: number; iterations?: number } = {}): VerletBody\n366\t```\n367\t\n368\tA rope from `from` to `to` in `segments` (the first particle pinned; `pinEnd` pins the last).\n369\t\n370\t### seeded()\n371\t\n372\t```ts\n373\tfunction seeded(seed: number): () => number\n374\t```\n375\t\n376\tA small seeded random number generator (mulberry32).\n377\t\n378\t### seesaw()\n379\t\n380\t```ts\n381\tfunction seesaw(ctx: Ctx, at: Vec3, o: SeesawOptions = {}): Built & { plank: RAPIER.RigidBody; hinge: RAPIER.RevoluteImpulseJoint }\n382\t```\n383\t\n384\tA plank on a hinge across its middle, on a wedge: weight on one end tips it.\n385\t\n386\t### interface SeesawOptions\n387\t\n388\t- `length?: number`: Plank length (m). Default 5.\n389\t- `width?: number`\n390\t- `height?: number`: Height of the pivot above `at` (m). Default 0.7.\n391\t- `yaw?: number`: Turn about Y (radians): 0 runs the plank along X.\n392\t- `tilt?: number`: Tilt limit either way (degrees). Default 16.\n393\t- `color?: PaletteColor`\n394\t\n395\t### softBlob()\n396\t\n397\t=== class SpriteBatch (line 4780)\n398\t### class SpriteBatch\n399\t\n400\t- `new SpriteBatch(sheet: SpriteSheet, o: { capacity: number })`\n401\t- `readonly sheet: SpriteSheet`\n402\t- `spawn(at: readonly [number, number, number], o: SpriteOptions = {}): number`: A new sprite (its index), or -1 when full.\n403\t- `set(i: number, o: SpriteOptions & { at?: readonly [number, number, number] }): void`: Move or change sprite `i`.\n404\t- `put(i: number, x: number, y: number, z: number, frame?: number, flip?: boolean): void`: `set` without the options object, for many sprites every frame: position, then frame and mirror.\n405\t- `at(i: number): [number, number, number]`: Where sprite `i` stands.\n406\t- `frameOf(i: number): number`: The frame sprite `i` shows.\n407\t- `dispose(): this`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance\n408\t\n409\t### interface SpriteOptions\n410\t\n411\t- `size?: number`: Height in metres (the width follows the frame's aspect). Default 1.\n412\t- `frame?: number`\n413\t- `flip?: boolean`: Mirror left-right (a sprite facing the other way).\n414\t\n415\t### interface SpriteSheet\n416\t\n417\t- `readonly texture: Texture`: The sheet (nearest-filtered); `drawSheet` makes one from code. Frames run left to right, top to bottom, from the image's top-left; a texture with `flipY` false (a `DataTexture`) holds its rows top line first.\n418\t- `readonly frame: readonly [number, number]`: Frame size in pixels and the frames across and down.\n419\t- `readonly cols: number`\n420\t- `readonly rows: number`\n421\t- `readonly frames: number`\n422\t\n423\t### swayMaterial()\n424\t\n425\t```ts\n426\tfunction swayMaterial(material: Material, wind: WindUniforms, o: SwayOptions): Material\n427\t```\n428\t\n429\tA room-owned copy of `material` that sways. For ordinary meshes: heights are in the mesh's\n430\town space (`positionGeometry`), measured from its origin (an instanced mesh would need its\n431\town per-instance base).\n432\t\n433\t=== drawSheet (line 4152)\n434\t### drawSheet()\n435\t\n436\t```ts\n437\tfunction drawSheet(o: { frame: readonly [number, number]; frames: number; cols?: number }, draw: (g: CanvasRenderingContext2D, frame: number) => void): SpriteSheet\n438\t```\n439\t\n440\tDraw a sheet in code: `draw(g, frame)` paints one frame into a `frame`-sized box (the\n441\tcontext is translated there and clipped). Pixel coordinates; draw with `fillRect`.\n442\t\n443\t### ease()\n444\t\n445\t```ts\n446\tfunction ease(e: Ease, u: number): number\n447\t```\n448\t\n449\t### type Ease\n450\t\n451\t```ts\n452\ttype Ease = EaseName | ((u: number) => number)\n453\t```\n454\t\n455\t### EASE_NAMES\n456\t\n457\t```ts\n458\tconst EASE_NAMES: EaseName[]\n459\t```\n460\t\n461\t### type EaseName\n462\t\n463\t```ts\n464\ttype EaseName = | 'linear' | 'inQuad' | 'outQuad' | 'inOutQuad' | 'inCubic' | 'outCubic' | 'inOutCubic' | 'inSine' | 'outSine' | 'inOutSine' | 'inExpo' | 'outExpo' | 'inOutExpo' | 'inBack' | 'outBack' | 'inOutBack' | 'outElastic' | 'outBounce' | 'smooth' | 'st\n465\t```\n466\t\n467\tTweens: numbers that glide to a value over time, for doors, lifts, pickups, menus and\n468\tpads. Game time (they pause, slow down and freeze with `engine.timeScale` and hitstops)\n469\t=== class Trail (line 4922)\n470\t### class Trail\n471\t\n472\t- `new Trail(o: TrailOptions = {})`\n473\t- `readonly capacity: number`\n474\t- `width: number`\n475\t- `life: number`\n476\t- `readonly head: Color`: Head and tail colours (live: `trail.head.setHex(...)`).\n477\t- `readonly tail: Color`\n478\t- `push(p: Vector3, time: number): void`: The trail's newest point (call every frame while it moves).\n479\t- `reset(): void`: Drop every point.\n480\t- `get length: number`: Points alive now.\n481\t- `update(time: number, camera: Camera): void`: Per frame: forget old points, rebuild the ribbon facing `camera`.\n482\t- `dispose(): void`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance.\n483\t\n484\t### interface TrailOptions\n485\t\n486\t- `points?: number`: Most points kept. Default 24.\n487\t- `width?: number`: Width at the head (m).\n488\t- `life?: number`: Seconds a point lasts. Default 0.35.\n489\t- `color?: number`: Head and tail colours (hex).\n490\t- `tail?: number`\n491\t- `minStep?: number`: A new point only after moving this far (m). Default 0.05.\n492\t\n493\t### TRANSITION_CELLS\n494\t\n495\t```ts\n496\tconst TRANSITION_CELLS: { readonly diamonds: 16; readonly blinds: 12; readonly dissolve: 3; readonly mosaic: 20; }\n497\t```\n498\t\n499\tArt pixels per diamond cell, blind band, dissolve block; the most a mosaic block grows to.\n500\t\n501\t### type TransitionKind\n502\t\n503\t```ts\n504\ttype TransitionKind = 'fade' | 'iris' | 'diamonds' | 'dissolve' | 'dither' | 'blinds' | 'wipe' | 'curtain' | 'mosaic'\n505\t=== hologramMaterial (line 4404)\n506\t### hologramMaterial()\n507\t\n508\t```ts\n509\tfunction hologramMaterial(o: ShaderOptions = {}): MeshBasicNodeMaterial\n510\t```\n511\t\n512\tA hologram: scanlines climbing the object, a bright rim where it turns away from you, a\n513\tflicker; the middle mostly see-through.\n514\t\n515\t### lavaMaterial()\n516\t\n517\t```ts\n518\tfunction lavaMaterial(o: ShaderOptions = {}): MeshBasicNodeMaterial\n519\t```\n520\t\n521\tLava: slow churning fractal noise, banded dark crust to white-hot, unlit (it glows).\n522\t\n523\t### interface Leaf\n524\t\n525\t- `at: V3`\n526\t- `dir: V3`: The way the twig it grows on points.\n527\t- `depth: number`\n528\t\n529\t### interface LRule\n530\t\n531\tOne right-hand side, chosen with probability `p` among a symbol's rules.\n532\t\n533\t- `to: string`\n534\t- `p?: number`\n535\t\n536\t### interface LSystemDef\n537\t\n538\t- `axiom: string`\n539\t- `rules: Readonly<Record<string, string | readonly LRule[]>>`: symbol → what replaces it (one string, or several to choose from by probability)\n540\t\n541\t=== glowMaterial (line 1192)\n542\t### glowMaterial()\n543\t\n544\t```ts\n545\tfunction glowMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation): MeshBasicNodeMaterial\n546\t```\n547\t\n548\tUnlit, full-bright material for a colour (flames, eyes, screens, crystal cores), shared and\n549\tcached per colour like `toonMaterial` (`userData.shared`; disposing it drops it from the\n550\tcache). Its vertices snap with the toon materials' under the `ps1` filter, so a glowing part\n551\tstays on its model.\n552\t\n553\t### LIGHT_POOL_SIZES\n554\t\n555\t```ts\n556\tconst LIGHT_POOL_SIZES: { readonly low: 4; readonly medium: 8; readonly high: 16; }\n557\t```\n558\t\n559\tPool sizes by quality level (`QUALITY[level].lights`).\n560\t\n561\t### class LightAssigner\n562\t\n563\tPure light assignment: `capacity` slots, many items. Each step picks the `capacity`\n564\thighest-scoring live items (items already holding a slot score × `hysteresis`, so two\n565\tsimilar requests don't trade a light back and forth), fades winners in and losers out,\n566\tand moves a slot to a new owner only once the old one has faded to 0. A fade changes a\n567\tlevel by at most `dt / fade` per step: nothing ever pops.\n568\t\n569\t- `new LightAssigner(capacity: number)`\n570\t- `readonly slots: (T | null)[]`: Slot → item holding it.\n571\t- `hysteresis: number`\n572\t- `get capacity: number`\n573\t- `resize(capacity: number, items: Iterable<T>): void`: Change the slot count (the pool's lights are rebuilt: a one-off shader recompile).\n574\t- `rank(it: T): number`: Effective rank of an item (score with the hysteresis bonus for holders).\n575\t- `step(dt: number, items: readonly T[]): AssignStats`\n576\t\n577\t=== class RenderView (line 4627)\n578\t### class RenderView\n579\t\n580\t- `new RenderView(o: RenderViewOptions = {})`\n581\t- `static screen(object: Object3D): void`: Put `object` (and its children) on the screens' layer.\n582\t- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n583\t- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n584\t- `every: number`: Render every nth frame.\n585\t- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n586\t- `enabled: boolean`\n587\t- `get texture: Texture`\n588\t- `setSize(w: number, h: number): void`: Resize the texture (the camera's aspect follows).\n589\t- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene): boolean`: Draw `scene` from the view's camera into its texture, if this is one of its frames. True if it drew.\n590\t- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`). Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs.\n591\t- `screenMaterial(): MeshBasicNodeMaterial`: An unlit material showing the view (a new one each call: tint it as you like).\n592\t- `dispose(): void`\n593\t\n594\t### interface RenderViewOptions\n595\t\n596\t- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Texture size in pixels (default [160, 90]).\n597\t- `fov?: number`: Vertical field of view, degrees (default 60).\n598\t- `near?: number`\n599\t- `far?: number`\n600\t- `every?: number`: Render every nth frame (default 1): a slow refresh costs less.\n601\t\n602\t### class Rng\n603\t\n604\tSeeded randomness. Everything random in a game comes from an `Rng`, so the same seed always\n605\tgives the same result (docs/DOCTRINE.md, principle 1). Each level gets one, `ctx.random`,\n606\tseeded from the engine's seed and the game's name; fork it by purpose so streams stay\n607\tindependent of how many numbers each one drew:\n608\t\n609\t  const level = ctx.random.fork(`level:${n}`);\n610\t  const room = level.fork(`room:${i}`);   // independent of how many numbers `level` drew\n611\t\n612\tNever use Math.random in game or engine code (the lint refuses it).\n613\t=== class Tweens (line 5023)\n614\t### class Tweens\n615\t\n616\tA set of running tweens (the engine keeps one per game: `ctx.tweens`).\n617\t\n618\t- `get count: number`: Tweens still running.\n619\t- `to(target: T, to: Partial<Record<keyof T, number>>, options: TweenOptions = {}): Tween`: Glide `target`'s numeric properties to `to`. A new tween on the same target and property takes over (the old one stops where it is).\n620\t- `value(from: number, to: number, options: TweenOptions, apply: (v: number) => void): Tween`: Tween a plain number from `from` to `to`, calling `apply(v)` every frame.\n621\t- `call(seconds: number, fn: () => void): Tween`: Call `fn` after `seconds` of game time.\n622\t- `cancel(target?: object): void`: Stop every tween on `target` (or everything).\n623\t- `clear(): void`: Stop everything (level unload). Pending `done` promises resolve.\n624\t- `update(dt: number): void`\n625\t\n626\t### interface View\n627\t\n628\t- `readonly container: HTMLElement | null`: The page element the canvas sits in; null headless.\n629\t- `readonly backend: BackendName`\n630\t- `readonly gpuErrors: readonly GpuErrorRecord[]`\n631\t- `readonly recoveries: number`: How many times a lost GPU device was recovered from (0 headless).\n632\t- `readonly lookVersion: number`: Counts look changes (UIs that mirror the look re-sync when it moves).\n633\t- `readonly screen: ScreenFx`: Transitions, flashes and shockwaves (`engine.screen`).\n634\t- `readonly viewport: Viewport`: The viewport the view is framed for (the container's size and the device pixel ratio).\n635\t- `readonly framing: Framing`\n636\t- `readonly resolution: Resolution`: The actual art resolution; adaptive varies its width, fill varies both dimensions.\n637\t- `readonly baseResolution: Resolution`: The configured resolution preset.\n638\t- `readonly aspect: AspectMode`\n639\t- `readonly mode: RenderMode`\n640\t- `readonly filters: readonly string[]`\n641\t- `readonly look: Look`: The current look (a copy).\n642\t- `readonly split: boolean`\n643\t- `readonly edges: EdgeSettings`\n644\t- `readonly activeCamera: Camera`\n645\t- `onRecovered: ((canvas: HTMLCanvasElement) => void) | null`: Called after a lost device was recovered with a new renderer and canvas.\n646\t- `onError: ((e: unknown) => void) | null`: Where a throwing `onBeforeRender` listener is reported.\n647\t- `setMode(mode: RenderMode): void`\n648\t- `toggleMode(): RenderMode`\n649\t=== class Squash (line 3817)\n650\t### class Squash\n651\t\n652\tSquash and stretch as a damped spring on `value` (0 = rest, + stretched, − squashed).\n653\t`scale()` turns it into a volume-preserving pair: `const [h, v] = squash.scale();\n654\tmesh.scale.set(h, v, h)`.\n655\t\n656\t- `value: number`\n657\t- `velocity: number`\n658\t- `stiffness: number`: Spring stiffness and damping (a critically damped spring has damping = 2√stiffness).\n659\t- `damping: number`\n660\t- `amount: number`: 0 turns it off; 2.5 is rubbery.\n661\t- `kick(v: number): void`: Add a kick: negative squashes (a landing), positive stretches (a jump).\n662\t- `set(v: number): void`: Set the shape directly (a held squash).\n663\t- `update(dt: number): void`\n664\t- `scale(out: [number, number] = [1, 1]): [number, number]`: [horizontal, vertical] scale: y = 1 + s, xz = 1 / √(1 + s), so the volume stays put.\n665\t\n666\t### twoBoneIK()\n667\t\n668\t```ts\n669\tfunction twoBoneIK(root: Vec3, target: Vec3, a: number, b: number, pole: Vec3, out: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0]): Vec3\n670\t```\n671\t\n672\tWhere the middle joint of a two-bone limb goes (a knee, an elbow) so the end reaches\n673\t`target` from `root` with bones `a` and `b` long, bending toward `pole` (a point the knee\n674\tpoints at). Analytic (the law of cosines), no iterations; a target out of reach straightens\n675\tthe limb toward it, one too close folds it as far as it goes. Returns the joint, into `out`.\n676\t\n677\t### validateClip()\n678\t\n679\t```ts\n680\tfunction validateClip(clip: ClipDef, rig: RigSpec): string[]\n681\t```\n682\t\n683\tProblems with a clip definition itself (unknown joints, bad key order, loop mismatch).\n684\t\n685\t=== class SpringChain (line 3795)\n686\t### class SpringChain\n687\t\n688\tA chain of points hanging off a moving root. Call `update(dt, root, basis)` every frame\n689\twith the root's world position and its orientation (three columns: right, up, forward),\n690\tthen read `points` (root first).\n691\t\n692\t- `new SpringChain(o: SpringChainOptions)`\n693\t- `readonly points: Vec3[]`\n694\t- `o: Required<SpringChainOptions>`\n695\t- `reset(root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`: Put the chain straight out in its rest pose (no swing).\n696\t- `update(dt: number, root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`\n697\t- `swing(basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): number`: How far the tip is from where the rest pose puts it (m): how much it is swinging.\n698\t\n699\t### interface SpringChainOptions\n700\t\n701\t- `segments: number`: Points after the root (≥ 1).\n702\t- `length: number`: Length of each segment (m).\n703\t- `rest?: Vec3`: Rest direction from the root in the root's own space (normalised; default straight back, −Z).\n704\t- `stiffness?: number`: Pull toward the rest pose per second (0 floppy … 30 stiff). Default 10.\n705\t- `keep?: number`: Velocity kept per 1/60 s (0..1). Default 0.94.\n706\t- `gravity?: number`: Gravity on the chain (m/s²). Default 6 (lighter than real: tails hold up a bit).\n707\t\n708\t### class Squash\n709\t\n710\tSquash and stretch as a damped spring on `value` (0 = rest, + stretched, − squashed).\n711\t`scale()` turns it into a volume-preserving pair: `const [h, v] = squash.scale();\n712\tmesh.scale.set(h, v, h)`.\n713\t\n714\t- `value: number`\n715\t- `velocity: number`\n716\t- `stiffness: number`: Spring stiffness and damping (a critically damped spring has damping = 2√stiffness).\n717\t- `damping: number`\n718\t- `amount: number`: 0 turns it off; 2.5 is rubbery.\n719\t- `kick(v: number): void`: Add a kick: negative squashes (a landing), positive stretches (a jump).\n720\t- `set(v: number): void`: Set the shape directly (a held squash).\n721\t=== class ParticlePool (line 2678)\n722\t### class ParticlePool\n723\t\n724\tFixed-size particle storage with CPU simulation. Alive particles are packed at the\n725\tfront (swap-remove), so the GPU draws exactly `alive` instances from one buffer.\n726\tPure (no three.js): unit-tested.\n727\t\n728\t- `new ParticlePool(preset: ParticlePreset)`\n729\t- `readonly max: number`\n730\t- `alive: number`\n731\t- `readonly pos: Float32Array`\n732\t- `readonly vel: Float32Array`\n733\t- `readonly age: Float32Array`\n734\t- `readonly life: Float32Array`\n735\t- `readonly size0: Float32Array`\n736\t- `readonly size1: Float32Array`\n737\t- `readonly colorSet: Uint8Array`: Index into `colorSets` per particle.\n738\t- `readonly colorSets: (readonly PaletteColor[])[]`: Color lists in use: [0] is the preset's, bursts with custom colors add more.\n739\t- `readonly preset: ParticlePreset`\n740\t- `spawn(at: Vec3, o: BurstOptions = {}, random: () => number = this.ownRandom): number`: Spawn a burst at `at`. Returns how many particles were spawned (the pool may be full). `random` in [0, 1): seeded, so bursts repeat.\n741\t- `step(dt: number): void`: Advance every particle by `dt` seconds and drop the dead ones.\n742\t- `t(i: number): number`: Life fraction 0..1 of particle `i`.\n743\t- `sizeAt(i: number): number`: Size in whole art pixels (0 = invisible).\n744\t- `colorAt(i: number): PaletteColor`: Current palette color name: stepped through the particle's color list.\n745\t- `clear(): void`\n746\t\n747\t### interface ParticlePreset\n748\t\n749\tA particle effect as data. Sizes are in art pixels (whole pixels, so particles stay crisp\n750\tsquares), colors are palette names stepped over each particle's life (no blending).\n751\t\n752\t- `count: Range`: Particles per burst.\n753\t- `life: Range`: Seconds each particle lives.\n754\t- `speed: Range`: Launch speed, world units / s.\n755\t- `direction?: Vec3`: Main launch direction (default straight up).\n756\t- `spread?: number`: Cone half-angle around `direction`, degrees (180 = every direction). Default 180.\n757\t=== class Particles (line 2727)\n758\t### class Particles\n759\t\n760\tPixel-art particles: CPU-simulated pools, drawn as camera-facing square sprites in flat\n761\tpalette colors. One emitter (one instanced draw call, one pooled instance buffer) per\n762\tpreset; sizes are whole art pixels, so in Pixel mode a particle is a crisp N×N block.\n763\tAvailable as `ctx.particles`; emitters are created on first use and freed by `clear()`\n764\t(the engine calls it when a level unloads).\n765\t\n766\t  ctx.particles.burst('dust', hero.feet);\n767\t  ctx.particles.burst('skid', feet, { direction: [-vx, 0.3, -vz], count: 2 });\n768\t\n769\t- `new Particles(view: () => ParticleView)`\n770\t- `readonly group: Group<Object3DEventMap>`: Engine-owned group holding every emitter.\n771\t- `readonly presets: Map<string, ParticlePreset>`: Preset registry: the built-ins plus anything registered.\n772\t- `readonly pixelWorld: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`: World units per art pixel at the camera focus (updated every frame).\n773\t- `register(name: string, preset: ParticlePreset): void`: Add or replace a named preset. Replacing frees the old preset's emitter.\n774\t- `burst(preset: string | ParticlePreset, at: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number], options: BurstOptions = {}): number`: Spawn a burst of `preset` (a name or a ParticlePreset) at `at`. Returns the number of particles spawned (fewer when the pool is ful\n775\t- `get alive: number`: Particles alive right now, over all emitters.\n776\t- `get emitterCount: number`: Emitters (= draw calls at most) currently allocated.\n777\t- `update(dt: number): void`: Simulate and upload. Called by the engine every frame (frozen while paused).\n778\t- `reseed(rng: Rng): void`: Take bursts' randomness from `rng` (the engine passes each level's `ctx.random` fork).\n779\t- `clear(): void`: Kill every particle and free the emitters (GPU buffers, materials).\n780\t- `dispose(): void`\n781\t\n782\t### PARTICLES\n783\t\n784\t```ts\n785\tconst PARTICLES: { dust: { count: [number, number]; life: [number, number]; speed: [number, number]; spread: number; flatten: number; gravity: number; drag: number; size: [number, number]; colors: (\"white\" | \"mist\" | \"slate\")[]; radius: number; }; skid: { ...;\n786\t```\n787\t\n788\tBuilt-in particle effects, as data (see ParticlePreset). Register more with\n789\t`ctx.particles.register(name, preset)`. Sizes are art pixels; colors are PALETTE names.\n790\t\n791\t## 10. HUD\n792\t\n793\t=== interface ParticlePreset (line 2703)\n794\t### interface ParticlePreset\n795\t\n796\tA particle effect as data. Sizes are in art pixels (whole pixels, so particles stay crisp\n797\tsquares), colors are palette names stepped over each particle's life (no blending).\n798\t\n799\t- `count: Range`: Particles per burst.\n800\t- `life: Range`: Seconds each particle lives.\n801\t- `speed: Range`: Launch speed, world units / s.\n802\t- `direction?: Vec3`: Main launch direction (default straight up).\n803\t- `spread?: number`: Cone half-angle around `direction`, degrees (180 = every direction). Default 180.\n804\t- `flatten?: number`: Multiply vertical launch speed (0.2 = dust that hugs the ground). Default 1.\n805\t- `gravity?: number`: Downward acceleration, world units / s² (negative floats up). Default 0.\n806\t- `drag?: number`: Velocity damping per second (0 = none).\n807\t- `size: readonly [number, number]`: Size in art pixels at birth and at death (rounded to whole pixels).\n808\t- `colors: readonly PaletteColor[]`: Palette colors stepped through over the lifetime.\n809\t- `radius?: number`: Random spawn offset radius, world units.\n810\t- `max?: number`: Pool size (max alive at once). Default 256.\n811\t\n812\t### type ParticlePresetName\n813\t\n814\t```ts\n815\ttype ParticlePresetName = keyof typeof PARTICLES\n816\t```\n817\t\n818\t### class Particles\n819\t\n820\tPixel-art particles: CPU-simulated pools, drawn as camera-facing square sprites in flat\n821\tpalette colors. One emitter (one instanced draw call, one pooled instance buffer) per\n822\tpreset; sizes are whole art pixels, so in Pixel mode a particle is a crisp N×N block.\n823\tAvailable as `ctx.particles`; emitters are created on first use and freed by `clear()`\n824\t(the engine calls it when a level unloads).\n825\t\n826\t  ctx.particles.burst('dust', hero.feet);\n827\t  ctx.particles.burst('skid', feet, { direction: [-vx, 0.3, -vz], count: 2 });\n828\t\n829\t=== class ScreenFx (line 4689)\n830\t### class ScreenFx\n831\t\n832\t- `cover(kind: TransitionKind = 'fade', o: TransitionOptions = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Cover the picture (progress → 1). Resolves when it stops: `true` when it is fully covered, `false` when another transition (or `set`, `clear`) took over first.\n833\t- `reveal(kind?: TransitionKind, o: TransitionOptions = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Uncover it (progress → 0) with `kind` (default: the one that covered it). Resolves like `cover`.\n834\t- `transition(kind: TransitionKind, between: () => unknown, o: TransitionOptions & { revealCenter?: TransitionOptions['center'] } = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Cover, run `between` (load a level, teleport), then reveal, also when `between` throws (the error is pas\n835\t- `set(kind: TransitionKind | null, progress: number): void`: Jump straight to a progress (0 clear, 1 covered), no animation.\n836\t- `flash(color: ScreenColor = 'white', o: FlashOptions = {}): void`: A full-screen flash that fades out.\n837\t- `shockwave(at: Vector3 | readonly [number, number], o: ShockwaveOptions = {}): void`: A ring that pushes the picture outwards from `at` (oldest ring is replaced when 4 run).\n838\t- `clear(): void`: Stop everything (a clear picture).\n839\t- `state(): ScreenFxState`\n840\t- `update(dt: number, camera: Camera | null): void`: Engine, every rendered frame (real seconds; `camera` projects world centres).\n841\t- `sampleNode(tex: any, scale: any): any`: Sample an art-resolution picture for the device pass, pushed by the shockwaves and blocked up by a mosaic transition, with the rings' bright edge. `tex` is the art target (a texture node); `scale` is device pixels per\n842\t- `colorNode(color: any, scale: any): any`: The transition and the flash over a finished colour (device pass).\n843\t\n844\t### interface ScreenFxState\n845\t\n846\tWhat `state()` reports (tests, tools).\n847\t\n848\t- `transition: TransitionKind | null`\n849\t- `progress: number`: 0 clear … 1 covered.\n850\t- `moving: boolean`: A transition is animating.\n851\t- `flash: number`\n852\t- `shockwaves: number`\n853\t\n854\t### interface ShaderOptions\n855\t\n856\t- `color?: number`\n857\t- `time?: any`: The clock it animates by (a float node). Default three's `time`, in seconds.\n858\t\n859\t### interface ShakeState\n860\t\n861\tA shake as data.\n862\t\n863\t- `readonly trauma: number`\n864\t- `readonly t: number`\n865\t=== interface LightRequestOptions (line 1281)\n866\t### interface LightRequestOptions\n867\t\n868\t- `position?: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number]`: World position (copied). Ignored while `follow` is set (then it is `follow` + `offset`).\n869\t- `follow?: Object3D | null`: Follow an object's world position every frame (a projectile, a monster, the hero).\n870\t- `offset?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Offset from `follow` (world axes).\n871\t- `color?: ColorRepresentation`\n872\t- `intensity?: number`: Point light intensity at full strength (before flicker and fades). Default 4.\n873\t- `radius?: number`: Reach in metres (PointLight.distance: light is 0 beyond it). Default 6.\n874\t- `decay?: number`: Distance falloff exponent (PointLight.decay; a uniform, free to change). Default 1.2.\n875\t- `flicker?: FlickerPreset`\n876\t- `priority?: number`: Importance multiplier: the hero's light 4, a loot beam 2, a torch 1 (default).\n877\t- `fadeIn?: number`: Fade times in seconds (defaults 0.25 in, 0.2 out).\n878\t- `fadeOut?: number`\n879\t- `lifetime?: number`: Release automatically after this many seconds (spell flashes, explosions).\n880\t- `name?: string`: Optional label for debugging (`pool.describe()`).\n881\t\n882\t### interface MergeOptions\n883\t\n884\t- `castShadow?: boolean`: Override castShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n885\t- `receiveShadow?: boolean`: Override receiveShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n886\t\n887\t### mergeStaticMeshes()\n888\t\n889\t```ts\n890\tfunction mergeStaticMeshes(sources: readonly Object3D[], options: MergeOptions = {}): Mesh[]\n891\t```\n892\t\n893\tMerge static meshes into one mesh per (material, shadow flags): N blocks with M\n894\tmaterials become ≤ M draw calls instead of N × groups (a BoxGeometry with 6 material\n895\tgroups is 6 draws, plus 6 more in the shadow pass).\n896\t\n897\tWorld transforms are baked into the vertices, multi-material geometry is split by its\n898\tgroups, and `position` + `normal` are kept, plus `uv` under a material with a `map` and\n899\t`color` under one with `vertexColors` (what toon materials read). The\n900\tsources are left untouched (don't add them to the scene). Physics is separate: keep\n901\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"4959bd49-44e2-445d-9c63-941615510cf6","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:22:29.931Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-max-plan-v2--20261104-211914--x044929-work/8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1/tool-results/bt23m2k02.txt","content":"=== class Timeline (line 4881)\n### class Timeline\n\n- `new Timeline(o: TimelineOptions)`\n- `readonly duration: number`\n- `time: number`: The playhead (s).\n- `playing: boolean`\n- `speed: number`: Playback rate (1: real time, 0.5: slow motion).\n- `ended: boolean`: True once the end has been reached (by playing or skipping).\n- `readonly fired: string[]`: Cue names in the order they fired (tests and tools).\n- `play(): void`\n- `pause(): void`\n- `update(dt: number): void`: Advance by `dt` seconds of game time (times `speed`) while playing, firing the cues passed.\n- `seek(t: number): void`: Move the playhead to `t` without firing the cues in between (scrubbing). Cues before `t` count as done and cues after it will fire again (going back re-arms them). Ignored while skipping (a cue that loops back cannot undo a skip).\n- `skip(): void`: Jump to the end: the cues not yet fired run (except the cosmetic ones), then `onEnd`. Cues after `duration` never fire, played or skipped.\n- `camera(t = this.time): CameraShot | null`: Where the camera is at `t` (default now): on each key at its time, gliding between keys on a smooth curve (Catmull-Rom tangents, so the speed has no jolt at a key; the first and last key of each shot ease in and ou\n- `line(t = this.time): Line | null`: The subtitle showing at `t` (default now), or null.\n- `bars(t = this.time): number`: How far the letterbox bars are in (0..1) at `t` (default now): sliding in at the start, out at the end.\n\n### interface TimelineLine\n\n- `at: number`\n- `until: number`\n- `text: string`\n- `who?: string`: Who is speaking (shown before the text).\n\n### interface TimelineOptions\n\n- `shots?: readonly CameraKey[]`\n- `cues?: readonly Cue[]`\n- `lines?: readonly Line[]`\n- `duration?: number`: Length (s); default the last key, cue or line.\n- `bars?: number`: Seconds the letterbox bars take to slide in and out (default 0.6; 0: no bars).\n- `onEnd?: () => void`: Called once when the playhead reaches the end (or the scene is skipped).\n\n### interface TraceRow\n=== interface TimelineOptions (line 4906)\n### interface TimelineOptions\n\n- `shots?: readonly CameraKey[]`\n- `cues?: readonly Cue[]`\n- `lines?: readonly Line[]`\n- `duration?: number`: Length (s); default the last key, cue or line.\n- `bars?: number`: Seconds the letterbox bars take to slide in and out (default 0.6; 0: no bars).\n- `onEnd?: () => void`: Called once when the playhead reaches the end (or the scene is skipped).\n\n### interface TraceRow\n\n- `name: string`\n- `kind: string`\n- `depth: number`\n- `status: Status | null`: This tick's answer, or null if this tick never reached the node.\n\n### class Trail\n\n- `new Trail(o: TrailOptions = {})`\n- `readonly capacity: number`\n- `width: number`\n- `life: number`\n- `readonly head: Color`: Head and tail colours (live: `trail.head.setHex(...)`).\n- `readonly tail: Color`\n- `push(p: Vector3, time: number): void`: The trail's newest point (call every frame while it moves).\n- `reset(): void`: Drop every point.\n- `get length: number`: Points alive now.\n- `update(time: number, camera: Camera): void`: Per frame: forget old points, rebuild the ribbon facing `camera`.\n- `dispose(): void`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance.\n\n### interface TrailOptions\n\n- `points?: number`: Most points kept. Default 24.\n- `width?: number`: Width at the head (m).\n- `life?: number`: Seconds a point lasts. Default 0.35.\n=== class Decals (line 4127)\n### class Decals\n\n- `new Decals(scene: Scene, o: { capacity?: number } = {})`\n- `readonly meshes: Map<\"ring\" | \"crack\" | \"footprint\" | \"scorch\" | \"splat\", InstancedMesh<BufferGeometry<NormalBufferAttributes, BufferGeometryEventMap>, Material<...> | Material…`\n- `readonly o: { capacity?: number }`\n- `add(shape: DecalShape, at: Vector3Like, normal: Vector3Like, o: DecalOptions = {}): number`: Lay a mark at `at` on a surface facing `normal`. Returns its index in that shape's pool.\n- `count(shape?: DecalShape): number`: Marks alive (per shape or all).\n- `update(dt: number): void`: Per frame: age the marks; old ones dither away over a second.\n- `clear(): void`: Remove every mark (the meshes stay for reuse).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### type DecalShape\n\n```ts\ntype DecalShape = (typeof DECAL_SHAPES)[number]\n```\n\n### decodeState()\n\n```ts\nfunction decodeState(v: unknown): unknown\n```\n\n`encodeState` undone: a deep copy with the marked numbers (and the game's own `@` strings) back.\n\n### drawSheet()\n\n```ts\nfunction drawSheet(o: { frame: readonly [number, number]; frames: number; cols?: number }, draw: (g: CanvasRenderingContext2D, frame: number) => void): SpriteSheet\n```\n\nDraw a sheet in code: `draw(g, frame)` paints one frame into a `frame`-sized box (the\ncontext is translated there and clipped). Pixel coordinates; draw with `fillRect`.\n\n### ease()\n=== interface DecalOptions (line 4120)\n### interface DecalOptions\n\n- `size?: number`: Width of the mark (m). Default 0.5.\n- `rotation?: number`: Turn about the normal (radians). Default random.\n- `color?: number`: Colour (hex). Default dark.\n- `life?: number`: Seconds before it starts to fade (0: forever). Default 10.\n\n### class Decals\n\n- `new Decals(scene: Scene, o: { capacity?: number } = {})`\n- `readonly meshes: Map<\"ring\" | \"crack\" | \"footprint\" | \"scorch\" | \"splat\", InstancedMesh<BufferGeometry<NormalBufferAttributes, BufferGeometryEventMap>, Material<...> | Material…`\n- `readonly o: { capacity?: number }`\n- `add(shape: DecalShape, at: Vector3Like, normal: Vector3Like, o: DecalOptions = {}): number`: Lay a mark at `at` on a surface facing `normal`. Returns its index in that shape's pool.\n- `count(shape?: DecalShape): number`: Marks alive (per shape or all).\n- `update(dt: number): void`: Per frame: age the marks; old ones dither away over a second.\n- `clear(): void`: Remove every mark (the meshes stay for reuse).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### type DecalShape\n\n```ts\ntype DecalShape = (typeof DECAL_SHAPES)[number]\n```\n\n### decodeState()\n\n```ts\nfunction decodeState(v: unknown): unknown\n```\n\n`encodeState` undone: a deep copy with the marked numbers (and the game's 