{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N4ndDAiGGmatvkpuJ6f6tD","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n/**\n * hub-check.mjs — does a game keep the AI Hub Session Protocol?\n *\n * Runs lib/hub/harness.html?auto=1 against each game, at the player counts its\n * hub:session-players allows: hello, ready under the hub's card with no key\n * press, the start, traffic, a player leaving, time-up and a valid result. Then\n * once more with the host leaving. Then the game on its own, outside a session:\n * it opens, Enter and Space are pressed, and it must draw its screen with no\n * errors, the session client inactive and Math.random left alone. Before any\n * game script runs, every frame in session mode gets alert, confirm, prompt,\n * window.open and socket constructors wrapped, so calling them is caught.\n * Needs Playwright, which is not a dependency (see shots.mjs).\n *\n * Parallel is played at 1 and 2 players: nothing is shared, so more copies\n * prove nothing more. Its checks expect Math.random seeded the same on every\n * copy, progress from every copy, and no game traffic.\n *\n * Ghost and shared world are played at 2, 3 and 4 players on a poor network\n * (150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss). Ghost is checked like parallel, except that every\n * copy sends its player. A shared world wants traffic both ways, and is\n * played once more at 2 players with its world hosted by one more copy that\n * has no player of its own, as a dedicated server would host it (README,\n * \"Shared world\"). That run is reported like any; --record does not hold it\n * against a game, since no server runs yet.\n *\n * --retrofit is for an existing game upgraded to parallel: it is played once,\n * at 2 players with one of them leaving. With --original <path>, errors the\n * original page already had are forgiven when it is opened on its own.\n * --draws-only does only that last part, for any page: the retrofit runs it on\n * a game before spending a model on it, since a page this browser cannot run\n * cannot be checked here. A WebGPU-only game without WebGPU is caught even\n * when its title screen shows: it asked for an adapter, got none, and drew\n * nothing with WebGL or a 2D canvas instead. --browser-args passes flags to\n * Chromium; on a machine without a GPU, SwiftShader gives such games a\n * software adapter:\n *   --browser-args \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader\"\n *\n * Every game's pasted client is also read from disk and must be exactly a\n * released one (scripts/lib/hub-client.mjs).\n *\n * --record writes the outcome into data/overrides.json, which is how the hub\n * keeps a failing game out of sessions: a game that fails gets \"session\": \"0\"\n * (it overrides the game's own hub:session meta, so Random Mode never deals\n * it) and a sessionNote naming what failed; a game that passes loses both.\n *\n * Usage:  node scripts/hub-check.mjs [game paths…] [--players 2,3,4] [--base URL] [--json] [--no-solo]\n *                                    [--retrofit [--original <path>]] [--draws-only] [--record] [--browser-args \"<flags>\"]\n *         (games default to the three examples in lib/hub/examples/)\n */\n\nimport { createServer } from 'node:http';\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\nimport { mkdir, readdir, readFile, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n\nimport { staticHandler } from './lib/serve.mjs';\nimport { modeOf, SELF_REPORTED } from '../lib/hub/round.js';\nimport { findClients } from './lib/hub-client.mjs';\n...\n8: * once more with the host leaving. Then the game on its own, outside a session:\n29: * original page already had are forgiven when it is opened on its own.\n37: *   --browser-args \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader\"\n174:const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH, args: ['--no-sandbox', '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required', ...browserArgs] });\n181:      if (!asJson) console.log(`${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}  ${game}  draws on its own`);\n233:        console.log(`${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}  ${game}  on its own`);\n266: * The game on its own: open it as someone at the wall would, press Enter and\n309:    check('on its own: the session client is there and inactive', after.hub && after.hub.active === false, JSON.stringify(after.hub));\n311:    check('on its own: Math.random is left alone', after.hub && after.hub.seeded !== true, JSON.stringify(after.hub));\n316:  check('on its own: this browser can run it', !noWebGPU, noWebGPU ? `it asked for WebGPU, this browser has no adapter, and drew nothing with WebGL or 2D instead (${asked})` : asked);\n317:  check('on its own: it draws its screen', after.drawn, `${after.bytes} bytes of screenshot, a blank screen is ${blank}`);\n319:  if (!bare) check(`on its own: no errors${before ? ' the original did not have' : ''}`, !fresh.length, fresh.slice(0, 3).join('; '));\n\nfile\t2486\tcouch/index.html\n15:  it (locally and on GitHub) in the same session. Never leave a local\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:scripts/hub-check.mjs: * once more with the host leaving. Then the game on its own, outside a session:\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:scripts/hub-check.mjs: * original page already had are forgiven when it is opened on its own.\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:README.md: If a game misbehaves in a frame, *Open on its own page* in its Details drawer\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:README.md: record, **F** favourites, **O** opens a game on its own page, **/** writes a\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:assets/js/filter.js: * no value for it (most games name no model) follows them on its own. Once\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:assets/js/filter.js: * stack. Inside one game, every attempt stands on its own.\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:lib/hub/README.md: the game runs as it does on its own.\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:docs/session-hub.md: | game | `answer` | `answer`: `ready` or `more` | on its own card, after the welcome, until `start` |\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:assets/js/ui/detail.js: 'Open on its own page'\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:lib/kit/touch.js: * reason is tracked on its own, so the kit's settings panel closing does\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:docs/multiplayer-plan.md: progress and a seeded start expected; and the game on its own compared\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:docs/multiplayer-plan.md: agent on its own copy of the game, spend capped, every failure put back);","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"57d2e333-7204-4c58-8af8-04fc87b0c3ea","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:04.476Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n/**\n * hub-check.mjs — does a game keep the AI Hub Session Protocol?\n *\n * Runs lib/hub/harness.html?auto=1 against each game, at the player counts its\n * hub:session-players allows: hello, ready under the hub's card with no key\n * press, the start, traffic, a player leaving, time-up and a valid result. Then\n * once more with the host leaving. Then the game on its own, outside a session:\n * it opens, Enter and Space are pressed, and it must draw its screen with no\n * errors, the session client inactive and Math.random left alone. Before any\n * game script runs, every frame in session mode gets alert, confirm, prompt,\n * window.open and socket constructors wrapped, so calling them is caught.\n * Needs Playwright, which is not a dependency (see shots.mjs).\n *\n * Parallel is played at 1 and 2 players: nothing is shared, so more copies\n * prove nothing more. Its checks expect Math.random seeded the same on every\n * copy, progress from every copy, and no game traffic.\n *\n * Ghost and shared world are played at 2, 3 and 4 players on a poor network\n * (150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss). Ghost is checked like parallel, except that every\n * copy sends its player. A shared world wants traffic both ways, and is\n * played once more at 2 players with its world hosted by one more copy that\n * has no player of its own, as a dedicated server would host it (README,\n * \"Shared world\"). That run is reported like any; --record does not hold it\n * against a game, since no server runs yet.\n *\n * --retrofit is for an existing game upgraded to parallel: it is played once,\n * at 2 players with one of them leaving. With --original <path>, errors the\n * original page already had are forgiven when it is opened on its own.\n * --draws-only does only that last part, for any page: the retrofit runs it on\n * a game before spending a model on it, since a page this browser cannot run\n * cannot be checked here. A WebGPU-only game without WebGPU is caught even\n * when its title screen shows: it asked for an adapter, got none, and drew\n * nothing with WebGL or a 2D canvas instead. --browser-args passes flags to\n * Chromium; on a machine without a GPU, SwiftShader gives such games a\n * software adapter:\n *   --browser-args \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader\"\n *\n * Every game's pasted client is also read from disk and must be exactly a\n * released one (scripts/lib/hub-client.mjs).\n *\n * --record writes the outcome into data/overrides.json, which is how the hub\n * keeps a failing game out of sessions: a game that fails gets \"session\": \"0\"\n * (it overrides the game's own hub:session meta, so Random Mode never deals\n * it) and a sessionNote naming what failed; a game that passes loses both.\n *\n * Usage:  node scripts/hub-check.mjs [game paths…] [--players 2,3,4] [--base URL] [--json] [--no-solo]\n *                                    [--retrofit [--original <path>]] [--draws-only] [--record] [--browser-args \"<flags>\"]\n *         (games default to the three examples in lib/hub/examples/)\n */\n\nimport { createServer } from 'node:http';\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\nimport { mkdir, readdir, readFile, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n\nimport { staticHandler } from './lib/serve.mjs';\nimport { modeOf, SELF_REPORTED } from '../lib/hub/round.js';\nimport { findClients } from './lib/hub-client.mjs';\n...\n8: * once more with the host leaving. Then the game on its own, outside a session:\n29: * original page already had are forgiven when it is opened on its own.\n37: *   --browser-args \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader\"\n174:const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH, args: ['--no-sandbox', '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required', ...browserArgs] });\n181:      if (!asJson) console.log(`${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}  ${game}  draws on its own`);\n233:        console.log(`${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}  ${game}  on its own`);\n266: * The game on its own: open it as someone at the wall would, press Enter and\n309:    check('on its own: the session client is there and inactive', after.hub && after.hub.active === false, JSON.stringify(after.hub));\n311:    check('on its own: Math.random is left alone', after.hub && after.hub.seeded !== true, JSON.stringify(after.hub));\n316:  check('on its own: this browser can run it', !noWebGPU, noWebGPU ? `it asked for WebGPU, this browser has no adapter, and drew nothing with WebGL or 2D instead (${asked})` : asked);\n317:  check('on its own: it draws its screen', after.drawn, `${after.bytes} bytes of screenshot, a blank screen is ${blank}`);\n319:  if (!bare) check(`on its own: no errors${before ? ' the original did not have' : ''}`, !fresh.length, fresh.slice(0, 3).join('; '));\n\nfile\t2486\tcouch/index.html\n15:  it (locally and on GitHub) in the same session. Never leave a local\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:scripts/hub-check.mjs: * once more with the host leaving. Then the game on its own, outside a session:\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:scripts/hub-check.mjs: * original page already had are forgiven when it is opened on its own.\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:README.md: If a game misbehaves in a frame, *Open on its own page* in its Details drawer\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:README.md: record, **F** favourites, **O** opens a game on its own page, **/** writes a\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:assets/js/filter.js: * no value for it (most games name no model) follows them on its own. Once\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:assets/js/filter.js: * stack. Inside one game, every attempt stands on its own.\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:lib/hub/README.md: the game runs as it does on its own.\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:docs/session-hub.md: | game | `answer` | `answer`: `ready` or `more` | on its own card, after the welcome, until `start` |\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:assets/js/ui/detail.js: 'Open on its own page'\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:lib/kit/touch.js: * reason is tracked on its own, so the kit's settings panel closing does\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:docs/multiplayer-plan.md: progress and a seeded start expected; and the game on its own compared\nmichaelcrosato/ai-hub:docs/multiplayer-plan.md: agent on its own copy of the game, spend capped, every failure put back);","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01N4ndDAiGGmatvkpuJ6f6tD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9FjD5t77mnxYSCpUck","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M76LVoVQRRczWgFs2Rnu7L","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 262,335p hub-check.mjs | cut -c1-210; sed -n 100,172p hub-check.mjs | cut -c1-200","description":"Read the on-its-own check and how the player counts are chosen"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3374,"cache_read_input_tokens":214455,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3374},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"ed672dd8-0c62-4eff-a5a4-482ebdc2ebfa","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:07.147Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9FirzhkMCWHZzYyeXL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01M76LVoVQRRczWgFs2Rnu7L":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211914__x044929/work/_research/hub && sed -n 262,335p hub-check.mjs | cut -c1-210; sed -n 100,172p hub-check.mjs | cut -c1-200","description":"Read the on-its-own check and how the player counts are chosen"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01M76LVoVQRRczWgFs2Rnu7L":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211914__x044929/work/_research/hub"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M76LVoVQRRczWgFs2Rnu7L","type":"tool_result","content":"  return { name, pass: copies[0].pristine, detail: copies[0].pristine ? copies[0].version : `${copies[0].version ?? 'unknown'} edited: paste lib/hub/session.js again` };\n}\n\n/**\n * The game on its own: open it as someone at the wall would, press Enter and\n * Space a few times, and see that it still runs: no errors (none beyond what\n * an original page already had), the client inactive and Math.random left\n * alone, and something drawn on the screen.\n */\nasync function stillWorks(game, before, { bare = false } = {}) {\n  const checks = [];\n  const check = (name, pass, detail = '') => checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\n  const visit = async (page) => {\n    const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 800 } });\n    await context.addInitScript(watch);\n    const tab = await context.newPage();\n    const errors = [];\n    tab.on('pageerror', (e) => errors.push(e.message));\n    await tab.goto(/^https?:/.test(page) ? page : `${base}${page}`);\n    await tab.waitForTimeout(2500);\n    for (const key of ['Enter', 'Space', 'Enter', 'Space']) {\n      await tab.keyboard.press(key).catch(() => {});\n      await tab.waitForTimeout(500);\n    }\n    await tab.waitForTimeout(2000);\n    const hub = await tab.evaluate(() => (window.AIHub ? { active: window.AIHub.active, seeded: window.AIHub.seeded } : null)).catch(() => null);\n    const gfx = await tab.evaluate(() => window.__gfx ?? null).catch(() => null);\n    // A WebGL or WebGPU canvas often reads back blank from a script, so look at the screen instead:\n    // a blank one compresses to almost nothing, so a PNG past a blank page's size means something is drawn.\n    const bytes = (await tab.screenshot({ type: 'png' }).catch(() => Buffer.alloc(0))).length;\n    await context.close();\n    return { errors, hub, bytes, gfx };\n  };\n  const blank = await (async () => {\n    const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 800 } });\n    const tab = await context.newPage();\n    await tab.setContent('<body style=\"margin:0;background:#000\"></body>');\n    const bytes = (await tab.screenshot({ type: 'png' })).length;\n    await context.close();\n    return bytes;\n  })();\n  const after = await visit(game);\n  // A line of text on a plain screen already adds about 2 KB; a uniform screen of any colour adds nothing.\n  after.drawn = after.bytes > blank + 1200;\n  const known = before ? new Set((await visit(before)).errors) : new Set();\n  const fresh = after.errors.filter((e) => !known.has(e));\n  if (!bare) {\n    check('on its own: the session client is there and inactive', after.hub && after.hub.active === false, JSON.stringify(after.hub));\n    // A client before 1.3.0 has no seeded flag: it never seeds.\n    check('on its own: Math.random is left alone', after.hub && after.hub.seeded !== true, JSON.stringify(after.hub));\n  }\n  const g = after.gfx;\n  const noWebGPU = g?.askedForWebGPU && !g.gotAdapter && !g.webgl && !g.twoD;\n  const asked = g ? `WebGPU ${g.askedForWebGPU ? (g.gotAdapter ? 'asked, adapter' : 'asked, no adapter') : 'not asked'}; WebGL ${g.webgl ? 'yes' : 'no'}; 2D ${g.twoD ? 'yes' : 'no'}` : 'not seen';\n  check('on its own: this browser can run it', !noWebGPU, noWebGPU ? `it asked for WebGPU, this browser has no adapter, and drew nothing with WebGL or 2D instead (${asked})` : asked);\n  check('on its own: it draws its screen', after.drawn, `${after.bytes} bytes of screenshot, a blank screen is ${blank}`);\n  // Drawing is all a bare page is asked: its own errors are the original's business.\n  if (!bare) check(`on its own: no errors${before ? ' the original did not have' : ''}`, !fresh.length, fresh.slice(0, 3).join('; '));\n  return { pass: checks.every((c) => c.pass), checks };\n}\n\n/**\n * Keep the verdict with the game: a failure takes it out of sessions until it\n * passes again (see the header). Games are found by path in data/games.json.\n */\nasync function recordChecks() {\n  let manifest;\n  try {\n    manifest = JSON.parse(await readFile(path.join(ROOT, 'data/games.json'), 'utf8'));\n  } catch {\n    console.log('--record needs data/games.json: run pnpm scan first');\n    return;\n  }\n  const slugOf = new Map();\n    const meta = (name) => html.match(new RegExp(`<meta\\\\s+name=[\"']${name}[\"']\\\\s+content=[\"']([^\"']+)[\"']`, 'i'))?.[1] ?? null;\n    const [least = 1, most = least] = (meta('hub:session-players')?.match(/\\d+/g) ?? []).map(Number);\n    return { mode: modeOf(meta('hub:session-mode')), seats: [least, most] };\n  } catch {\n    return { mode: null, seats: [1, 4] };\n  }\n}\n\nlet chromium;\ntry {\n  ({ chromium } = createRequire(import.meta.url)('playwright'));\n} catch {\n  console.error('hub-check needs Playwright: pnpm add -D playwright && pnpm exec playwright install chromium');\n  process.exit(2);\n}\n\n/**\n * Runs in every frame before its own scripts: it notes what the page asks of\n * the graphics stack, and session-mode pages are watched for dialogs and sockets.\n */\nfunction watch() {\n  // What the page asked of the graphics stack: a WebGPU adapter it never got, and\n  // no WebGL drawing instead, means this browser cannot run it (a title screen may still show).\n  const gfx = (window.__gfx = { askedForWebGPU: false, gotAdapter: false, webgl: false, twoD: false });\n  if (navigator.gpu?.requestAdapter) {\n    const ask = navigator.gpu.requestAdapter.bind(navigator.gpu);\n    Object.defineProperty(navigator.gpu, 'requestAdapter', {\n      configurable: true,\n      writable: true,\n      value: async (...a) => {\n        gfx.askedForWebGPU = true;\n        const adapter = await ask(...a);\n        if (adapter) gfx.gotAdapter = true;\n        return adapter;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n  for (const Canvas of [window.HTMLCanvasElement, window.OffscreenCanvas].filter(Boolean)) {\n    const getContext = Canvas.prototype.getContext;\n    Canvas.prototype.getContext = function (type, ...rest) {\n      const context = getContext.call(this, type, ...rest);\n      if (context && /^(webgl2?|experimental-webgl)$/.test(type)) gfx.webgl = true;\n      if (context && type === '2d') gfx.twoD = true;\n      return context;\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (!/[?&]aihub=/.test(location.search)) return;\n  const seen = (window.__hubViolations = []);\n  for (const name of ['alert', 'confirm', 'prompt', 'open']) {\n    window[name] = () => {\n      seen.push(`${name}() called`);\n      return name === 'confirm' ? false : null;\n    };\n  }\n  for (const name of ['WebSocket', 'RTCPeerConnection', 'EventSource']) {\n    const Original = window[name];\n    if (!Original) continue;\n    window[name] = function (...a) {\n      seen.push(`${name} opened in a session (${String(a[0]).slice(0, 80)})`);\n      return new Original(...a);\n    };\n  }\n  addEventListener('error', (e) => seen.push(`error: ${e.message}`));\n  addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (e) => seen.push(`unhandled rejection: ${e.reason?.message || e.reason}`));\n}\n\nlet server = null;\nif (!base) {\n  server = createServer(staticHandler(ROOT));\n  await new Promise((resolve) => server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', resolve));\n  base = `http://127.0.0.1:${server.address().port}`;\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"6ffb0af5-862e-487d-af8a-a735969766d9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:07.205Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  return { name, pass: copies[0].pristine, detail: copies[0].pristine ? copies[0].version : `${copies[0].version ?? 'unknown'} edited: paste lib/hub/session.js again` };\n}\n\n/**\n * The game on its own: open it as someone at the wall would, press Enter and\n * Space a few times, and see that it still runs: no errors (none beyond what\n * an original page already had), the client inactive and Math.random left\n * alone, and somethi