{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AX8bfY7e9He8qi5z5AEPtY","type":"tool_result","content":"## 12. Animation toolkit\n\n### analyzeClip()\n\n```ts\nfunction analyzeClip(model: Object3D, rig: RigSpec, def: ClipDef, clip: AnimationClip): ClipReport\n```\n\n### interface ClipDef\n\n- `name: string`\n- `frames: number`: Length in frames at 30 fps.\n- `loop?: boolean`\n- `keys: readonly Key[]`\n- `layers?: readonly Layer[]`\n- `feet?: readonly FeetKey[]`: Feet track: foot goals interpolated between its own keys and solved with IK every frame, overriding the keyed leg rotations. Use it whenever feet touch the floor through a transition (kneel → stand, sit → lie) so they roll instea\n- `speed?: number`: Ground speed (m/s) the clip is authored for at playback rate 1. Locomotion clips set this; metrics then measure foot sliding against it and the runtime can scale playback.\n- `stance?: number`: Gait cycles (gaitClip): the share of the cycle each foot is planted. The right heel strikes at phase 0, the left at 0.5, so the right foot is mid-stance at `stance / 2`.\n- `reach?: number`: Gaits: how far ahead of the hips (m) the middle of the stance is (feet touch down `reach` + half a stance's ground ahead).\n- `grounded?: boolean`: Grounded clip: soles should rest on y = 0 (metrics flag floating / penetration).\n- `fast?: boolean`: Intentionally snappy (flips, punches, launches): skip the angular-speed warning.\n- `notes?: string`\n\n### interface ClipReport\n\nObjective checks for a clip, computed by actually posing the rig (no renderer). These\nare the numbers an agent can't eyeball: foot sliding, ground contact, loop seams,\nvelocity spikes, joint limits. Thresholds are deliberately forgiving; `problems` are\nreal defects, `warnings` are worth a look.\n\n- `name: string`\n- `frames: number`\n3764:### interface RigSpec\n3765-\n3766-Everything the tools need to know about a rig beyond its hierarchy.\n3767-\n3768-- `joints: readonly string[]`: Joint names in hierarchy order (root first).\n3769-- `root: string`\n3770-- `mirror: Readonly<Record<string, string>>`: Left/right counterparts for mirroring.\n3771-- `soles: readonly string[]`: Mesh names that touch the ground (soles).\n3772-- `trace: readonly string[]`: Points to trace in contact sheets (joint or mesh names).\n3773-- `limits: Readonly<Record<string, JointLimit>>`: Human-plausible rotation ranges, degrees.\n3774-- `fps: number`: Frame rate of the authoring format.\n3775-- `legs?: LegRig`: Leg geometry, enabling foot IK and the gait generator.\n3776-- `spine?: { torso?: string; head?: string; cap?: string }`: Joints the runtime procedural layers turn (PoseLayers): the torso and head look where the character is going; `cap` is an optional springy joint (not animated by clips).\n3777-\n3778-### sampleClip()\n3779-\n3780-```ts\n3547:### interface ClipDef\n3548-\n3549-- `name: string`\n3550-- `frames: number`: Length in frames at 30 fps.\n3551-- `loop?: boolean`\n3552-- `keys: readonly Key[]`\n3553-- `layers?: readonly Layer[]`\n3554-- `feet?: readonly FeetKey[]`: Feet track: foot goals interpolated between its own keys and solved with IK every frame, overriding the keyed leg rotations. Use it whenever feet touch the floor through a transition (kneel → stand, sit → lie) so they roll i\n3555-- `speed?: number`: Ground speed (m/s) the clip is authored for at playback rate 1. Locomotion clips set this; metrics then measure foot sliding against it and the runtime can scale playback.\n3556-- `stance?: number`: Gait cycles (gaitClip): the share of the cycle each foot is planted. The right heel strikes at phase 0, the left at 0.5, so the right foot is mid-stance at `stance / 2`.\n3557-- `reach?: number`: Gaits: how far ahead of the hips (m) the middle of the stance is (feet touch down `reach` + half a stance's ground ahead).\n3558-- `grounded?: boolean`: Grounded clip: soles should rest on y = 0 (metrics flag floating / penetration).\n3559-- `fast?: boolean`: Intentionally snappy (flips, punches, launches): skip the angular-speed warning.\n3560-- `notes?: string`\n3561-\n3562-### interface ClipReport\n3563-\n3597:### compileClips()\n3598-\n3599-```ts\n3600-function compileClips(defs: readonly ClipDef[], rig: RigSpec, model: Object3D): AnimationClip[]\n3601-```\n3602-\n3603-### interface Foot\n3604-\n3605-- `readonly at: Vec3`: World position of the foot now.\n3606-- `t: number`: Stepping: 0 → 1 through the step; -1 planted.\n3607-- `readonly from: Vec3`\n3608-- `readonly to: Vec3`\n3609-\n## 13. Hero kit\n\n### HERO_CLIPS\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_CLIPS: readonly ClipDef[]\n```\n\n### HERO_MODEL\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_MODEL: \"assets/hero.glb\"\n```\n\n### HERO_RAGDOLL\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_RAGDOLL: readonly RagdollPart[]\n```\n\nThe hero as a ragdoll (the joints of `hero.glb`, see rig.ts): pelvis, torso and head, upper\narms and legs on ball joints held in cones, elbows and knees as hinges bending the way the\nclips bend them (Forearm −X, Shin +X). Hands and feet ride on their forearm and shin.\n\n### HERO_RIG\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_RIG: RigSpec\n```\n\nThe hero rig (public/assets/hero.glb, built by scripts/assets/hero.mjs).\n\nThe character faces +Z. L/R are the character's own sides (its right = -X).\nRotations are Euler XYZ degrees relative to rest; Z is applied first, then Y, then X,\nall about the parent's axes. Verified against contact sheets (`npm run anim -- sheet`).\n\n  Pelvis   +X tip forward (90 = face down, -90 = on its back, 360 = front flip)\n           +Y turn to its left, +Z roll to its RIGHT. p = [x, y, z] offset (m), s = squash\n  Torso    +X bend forward, +Y twist left, +Z lean right\n  Head     +X look down, +Y look left, +Z tilt right\n  Arm*     X swings: -90 = straight ahead, -180 = overhead, +40 = back\n           Z spreads (…\n\n## 14. three.js and Rapier\nmaster:.8,sfx:1,music:.6,muted:!1\nin:.55,decay:.3,volume:.24}},MK=e=>2e4*(400/2e4)**Math.max(0,Math.min(1,e)),NK=`pixel-engine:audio`,PK={master: