{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S3haormWjUvyExzEezvDpr","type":"tool_result","content":"9:3. Rendering, looks and filters: `AMOUNT`, `applyFilter`, `applyFilters`, `BackendName`, `CapturedFrame`, `clampParam`, `cloneLook`, `DEFAULT_EDGES`, `DEFAULT_PIXEL`, `defaultLook`, `defaultParams`, `EdgeSettings`, `FILTER_IDS`, `FILTER_PRESETS`, `FilterContext`, `FilterDef`, `FilterGroup`, `filterOrder`, `FilterParam`, `filterParams`, `filterPresetOf`, `filterPresets`, `FILTERS`, `FilterSpace`, `getFilter`, `LayerLook`, `Look`, `LOOK_ALIASES`, `LOOK_PRESETS`, `LOOK_TARGET_LABELS`, `LOOK_TARGETS`, `LookFilter`, `lookFilters`, `lookFromFilters`, `LookLayer`, `lookLayerOf`, `LookPlan`, `lookPresetLabel`, `lookPresetName`, `lookPresetOf`, `looksEqual`, `LookTarget`, `NO_WEBGPU`, `normalizeLook`, `PALETTES`, `paramsOf`, `PIXEL_PARAMS`, `PIXEL_PRESETS`, `PixelLook`, `PixelRenderer`, `planLook`, `RenderMode`, `scenePixel`, `setLookLayer`, `splitFilters`\n17:11. Models and textures (ASSETS.md): `addModelColliders`, `around`, `assetProgress`, `AssetReader`, `BakedTexture`, `bakeTexture`, `boxFrame`, `buildModel`, `Catalog`, `CatalogEntry`, `checkModel`, `decodePng`, `DEFAULT_TEXEL`, `ExpandedModel`, `expandModel`, `gridOf`, `groupVariants`, `hudSprite`, `ImportError`, `importSheet`, `LICENCES`, `loadModel`, `loadPack`, `loadPackIndex`, `meanColour`, `model`, `Model`, `MODEL_FAMILIES`, `MODEL_LIBRARY`, `ModelBinding`, `ModelBuild`, `ModelCatalog`, `ModelCheck`, `ModelCollider`, `ModelDef`, `ModelError`, `ModelLight`, `ModelLightRequest`, `ModelOptions`, `ModelPack`, `ModelPart`, `ModelProvenance`, `modelSheet`, `ModelSheet`, `ModelSheetOptions`, `MOVING_TEXEL`, `PackIndex`, `PackIndexEntry`, `packTextures`, `parsePack`, `PngError`, `preloadModels`, `RgbaImage`, `rowOf`, `scatterOf`, `searchDefs`, `SearchHit`, `searchHits`, `SearchOptions`, `searchWords`, `setAssetReader`, `SheetImport`, `SheetImportOptions`, `spriteSheet`, `TEXTURE_FAMILIES`, `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`, `TextureCatalog`, `TextureCheck`, `textureDef`, `TextureDef`, `TextureError`, `TextureLayer`, `textureMap`, `textureSheet`, `TextureSheet`, `TextureSheetOptions`, `validateModel`, `validateTexture`, `VariantGroup`, `variantName`\n868:### interface LayerLook\n934:### type LookLayer\n937:type LookLayer = 'actors' | 'environment'\n## 10. HUD\n\n### class Hud\n\nPixel HUD: crisp text and icons drawn in art pixels on top of the game, never through\nthe post filters. It is a 2D canvas at the internal resolution (480×270 / 320×180),\nlaid over the game canvas with the same integer scale and letterbox offset\n(`framing.ts`), so one HUD pixel is exactly one art pixel at every resolution.\n\nRetained: what you add stays on screen until `clear()`. Redraw everything each frame\n(clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\nresolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\n\n  ctx.hud.clear();\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\n\n- `new Hud(container: HTMLElement | null)`\n- `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`: The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn).\n- `visible: boolean`\n- `get width: number`: HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution).\n- `get height: number`\n- `text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation).\n- `rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor: HudAnchor = 'top-left'): void`: A filled rectangle (panels, bars).\n- `sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = t\n- `clear(): void`: Remove everything.\n- `measure(text: string, scale = 1): { width: number; height: number }`: Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`.\n- `sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void`: Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed.\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### type HudAnchor\n\n```ts\ntype HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right'\n```\n\nWhere an element is attached on screen; it is also aligned that way (right-anchored text grows left).\n\n### type HudColor\n\n```ts\ntype HudColor = PaletteColor | number\n```\n\n### interface HudOptions\n\n- `color?: HudColor`: Default 'white'.\n- `shadow?: HudColor | false`: 1-pixel drop shadow color, or false. Default 'ink'.\n- `scale?: number`: Integer art-pixel scale (2 = double-size glyphs). Default 1.\n- `anchor?: HudAnchor`: Default 'top-left': x/y are offsets from that screen corner/edge, in art pixels.\n\n### hudPlace()\n\n```ts\nfunction hudPlace(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, anchor: HudAnchor, size: Resolution): [number, number]\n```\n\nTop-left corner, in whole art pixels, of a w×h element placed at offset (x, y) from\n`anchor` on a screen of `size` art pixels. Pure (unit-tested).\n\n## 11. Models and textures (ASSETS.md)\n2462:### class AudioManager\n2582:### interface Song\n4152:### drawSheet()\n2462:### class AudioManager\n2463-\n2464-Web Audio for games: procedural retro sound effects (`SFX`, data), a small chiptune\n2465-sequencer (`Song`, data), optional audio files, and master / sfx / music volume + mute\n2466-persisted in localStorage. Available as `ctx.audio`.\n2467-\n2468-Browsers only allow sound after a user gesture, so the AudioContext is created on the\n2469-first key / pointer / touch input. Before that, and wherever Web Audio does not exist\n2470-(headless tests, old browsers), every call is a silent no-op that still records what","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"7d