{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBAqyxtrYzqnZWKLZqy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lj6sSygjoGxPa644nVhZ39","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211914__x044929/work/_research/engine/pixel-engine && for s in \"### loadPack\" \"### parsePack\" \"### setAssetReader\" \"### interface ModelBuild\" \"### hudSprite\" \"### loadPackIndex\" \"### interface HeadlessOptions\" \"### interface TouchButton\" ; do n=$(grep -n \"^$s\" API.md | head -1 | cut -d: -f1); echo \"=== $s ($n)\"; sed -n \"$n,$((n+16))p\" API.md | cut -c1-280; done; grep -n \"slab\\|lathe\" LIBRARY.md | head -3 | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"slab:\" -r examples/*.js | head; node -e \"\nconst lib=require('./library.json');\nconst a=lib.assets.filter(x=>/hospital|clinic|medical|monitor|television|computer|screen|curtain|sink|shower|toilet|door|window|coat|plant|bookcase|lamp|rug|stool|trash|fridge|laptop|desk/i.test(x.id));\nconsole.log(a.length); console.log(a.map(x=>x.id).join(' ').slice(0,3200));\nconsole.log(lib.packs.map(p=>p.id||p).join(' '));\n\"","description":"Read pack loading APIs and list useful furniture props"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1194,"cache_read_input_tokens":324049,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1194},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"a62be76d-0d85-45ea-be91-43df9ff7e3cc","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:48:23.162Z","request_id":"req_011CgjBAqjLid5oJV7PecDg2","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Lj6sSygjoGxPa644nVhZ39":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211914__x044929/work/_research/engine/pixel-engine && for s in \"### loadPack\" \"### parsePack\" \"### setAssetReader\" \"### interface ModelBuild\" \"### hudSprite\" \"### loadPackIndex\" \"### interface HeadlessOptions\" \"### interface TouchButton\" ; do n=$(grep -n \"^$s\" API.md | head -1 | cut -d: -f1); echo \"=== $s ($n)\"; sed -n \"$n,$((n+16))p\" API.md | cut -c1-280; done; grep -n \"slab\\|lathe\" LIBRARY.md | head -3 | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"slab:\" -r examples/*.js | head; node -e \"\nconst lib=require('./library.json');\nconst a=lib.assets.filter(x=>/hospital|clinic|medical|monitor|television|computer|screen|curtain|sink|shower|toilet|door|window|coat|plant|bookcase|lamp|rug|stool|trash|fridge|laptop|desk/i.test(x.id));\nconsole.log(a.length); console.log(a.map(x=>x.id).join(' ').slice(0,3200));\nconsole.log(lib.packs.map(p=>p.id||p).join(' '));\n\"","description":"Read pack loading APIs and list useful furniture props"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lj6sSygjoGxPa644nVhZ39","type":"tool_result","content":"=== ### loadPack (3022)\n### loadPack()\n\n```ts\nfunction loadPack(url: string, opts: { readonly into?: ModelCatalog; readonly textures?: TextureCatalog } = {}): Promise<ModelCatalog>\n```\n\nLoad a pack of imported models and textures (`public/packs/<pack>.json`, docs/assets/importing.md\n*Packs*) once, the way `loadModel` loads a GLB: the URL resolved the same way (under the\nbase URL; a page may put a data URL for it in `__PIXEL_ASSETS__`, as single-file builds do for\nevery `packs/<id>.json` path the built code names, cut to the models it names), counted by\n`assetProgress`. Resolves to a catalog of the\npack's ModelDefs, to build from with `buildModel(id, { catalog })`; `into` also adds them to a\ncatalog of yours (e.g. `MODEL_LIBRARY`, so `use` finds them), and `textures` gets the pack's\nTextureDefs (e.g. `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`, so `textureMap(id)` and `hudSprite(id)` find them).\n\n### loadPackIndex()\n\n=== ### parsePack (3273)\n### parsePack()\n\n```ts\nfunction parsePack(data: unknown, where = 'pack'): ModelPack\n```\n\nCheck a pack file's shape (the models' and textures' own checks are `validateModel`'s and `validateTexture`'s).\n\n### class PngError\n\nA PNG the decoder can't read, with what is wrong.\n\n- `new PngError(message: string)`\n\n### preloadModels()\n\n```ts\n=== ### setAssetReader (3366)\n### setAssetReader()\n\n```ts\nfunction setAssetReader(read: AssetReader | null): void\n```\n\nWhere models and packs come from, for the whole process (`loadModel` and `loadPack` share one\ncache): a reader, or null for the page's way (fetch under the base URL). Loads already made stay cached.\n\n### interface SheetImport\n\n- `readonly defs: readonly TextureDef[]`\n- `readonly colours: readonly SheetColour[]`: Every distinct opaque source colour of the imported cells, biggest first.\n- `readonly merges: readonly SheetMerge[]`: Every PALETTE entry two or more of those colours bake as, biggest first.\n- `readonly map: ColourMap`: The mapper's result (slots and their entries, before `palette` re-binds them).\n- `readonly cells: readonly SheetCell[]`: Every cell of the grid, in reading order.\n- `readonly columns: number`\n=== ### interface ModelBuild (3094)\n### interface ModelBuild\n\n- `readonly id: string`\n- `readonly object: Group`: Named after the model; pivots are named Groups inside it.\n- `readonly bounds: Bounds`\n- `readonly anchors: Readonly<Record<string, { readonly at: Vec3; readonly rot: Vec3 }>>`\n- `readonly colliders: readonly ColliderData[]`\n- `readonly light: ModelLightRequest | null`\n- `readonly report: ModelReport`\n\n### class ModelCatalog\n\nModels by id: the engine's built-in library (`MODEL_LIBRARY`) or a game's own. `use` parts\nand `buildModel('id')` resolve ids through one (the library unless a build passes another);\na game adds its models to the library, or builds a catalog of its own on top of it.\n\n- `new ModelCatalog(defs: readonly ModelDef[] = [])`\n=== ### hudSprite (2982)\n### hudSprite()\n\n```ts\nfunction hudSprite(idOrDef: string | TextureDef, o: TextureOptions & { frame?: number } = {}): { rows: string[]; colors: Record<string, PaletteColor | number> }\n```\n\nOne frame as `hud.sprite` rows and colours: a character per slot (a, b, c, … in palette order),\n'.' for transparent.\n\n  const s = hudSprite('gem-icon'); hud.sprite(8, 8, s.rows, s.colors, { scale: 2 });\n\n### class ImportError\n\nA file the importer can't read, with what is wrong and what to do.\n\n- `new ImportError(message: string)`\n\n=== ### loadPackIndex (3037)\n### loadPackIndex()\n\n```ts\nfunction loadPackIndex(url = 'packs/index.json'): Promise<PackIndex>\n```\n\nThe packs a site carries (`public/packs/index.json`, written by the importers): each pack's\nid, title, file (relative to the index), how many models and textures it holds, its licence\nand author. Load one with `loadPack(new URL(entry.file, indexUrl))`, or `packs/<file>`.\n\n### meanColour()\n\n```ts\nfunction meanColour(b: BakedTexture): number\n```\n\nThe mean colour of the opaque texels (0xrrggbb, sRGB): what a textured surface reads as from afar.\n=== ### interface HeadlessOptions (305)\n### interface HeadlessOptions\n\n`Engine.headless`: the page's options (those about the page do nothing), and where it runs.\n\n- `viewport?: Viewport`: The viewport the art resolution and framing come from, as a page's would (default 960×540 at DPR 1). Pointer aim and HUD layout depend on it: a replay uses its recording's (`Recording.view`).\n- `assets?: AssetReader`: How models and packs are read: `nodeAssets()` (src/engine/node.ts) reads `public/`.\n\n### class LoadingScreen\n\nMinimal pixel-styled loading indicator: a blocky segmented bar and a status word,\nplain DOM (it shows before the renderer exists). Reuses a `.pixel-loading` element\nalready in the container (index.html ships one so it appears before any JS runs).\n\n- `new LoadingScreen(container: HTMLElement, segments = 12)`\n- `readonly root: HTMLElement`\n- `set(progress: number, label?: string): void`: `progress` 0..1; `label` is shown in capitals.\n- `done(): void`\n=== ### interface TouchButton (2402)\n### interface TouchButton\n\n- `label: string`\n- `code: string`: Key code this button presses (e.g. 'Space').\n- `hint?: string`: Short hint shown under the label.\n- `at?: { x: number; y: number; size?: number; corner?: TouchCorner }`: Place the button yourself instead of in the default grid: its centre, in CSS pixels from `corner` (default bottom-right; `x` grows inward from the side, `y` inward from the top or bottom edge), and its diamet\n\n### interface TouchButtonState\n\nWhat a button shows right now (`TouchControls.set`): a game drives its buttons from its own\nstate each frame (skill icons, cooldowns, costs, a contextual action). Only what changed\ntouches the DOM.\n\n- `label?: string`\n- `hint?: string`\n- `icon?: HTMLCanvasElement | HTMLImageElement | null`: A picture instead of the label (a canvas or image; drawn pixelated); null removes it.\n- `cooldown?: number`: Cooldown shutter, 0..1 of the button covered (0 = ready).\n20:| `roof` | 4.7 × 1.73 × 3.73 | width 4 (1.5–10), depth 3 (1.5–8), pitch 40 (15–60) | tile red, tile2 plum, stone mist, wood orange | architecture, roof, stone, wood | Gable roof to sit on walls (y \n73:| `altar` | 1.9 × 1.02 × 1.12 | w 1.6 (1–2.4) | stone mist, stone2 slate, dark night, cloth red, trim sand | dungeon, stone, cloth, temple | Stone altar on a step: a pale slab top over a dark mould\n75:| `tombstone` | 0.81 × 1.04 × 0.38 | shape 0 (0–2), h 0.9 (0.6–1.3) | stone mist, stone2 slate, carve night, moss green | dungeon, stone, grave | Headstone on a low base with a tuft of moss (map `m\n105\ndoor window doorway wide-window trapdoor stool desk rug folding-screen lamp-post planter kenney-castle/door kenney-castle/tower-square-mid-door kenney-castle/tower-square-mid-windows kenney-castle/tower-square-top-roof-high-windows kenney-castle/wall-doorway kenney-furniture/bathroom-sink kenney-furniture/bathroom-sink-square kenney-furniture/bookcase-closed kenney-furniture/bookcase-closed-doors kenney-furniture/bookcase-closed-wide kenney-furniture/bookcase-open kenney-furniture/bookcase-open-low kenney-furniture/cabinet-television kenney-furniture/cabinet-television-doors kenney-furniture/chair-desk kenney-furniture/coat-rack kenney-furniture/coat-rack-standing kenney-furniture/computer-keyboard kenney-furniture/computer-mouse kenney-furniture/computer-screen kenney-furniture/desk kenney-furniture/desk-corner kenney-furniture/doorway kenney-furniture/doorway-front kenney-furniture/doorway-open kenney-furniture/kitchen-fridge kenney-furniture/kitchen-fridge-built-in kenney-furniture/kitchen-fridge-large kenney-furniture/kitchen-fridge-small kenney-furniture/kitchen-sink kenney-furniture/lamp-round-floor kenney-furniture/lamp-round-table kenney-furniture/lamp-square-ceiling kenney-furniture/lamp-square-floor kenney-furniture/lamp-square-table kenney-furniture/lamp-wall kenney-furniture/laptop kenney-furniture/plant-small1 kenney-furniture/plant-small2 kenney-furniture/plant-small3 kenney-furniture/potted-plant kenney-furniture/rug-doormat kenney-furniture/rug-rectangle kenney-furniture/rug-round kenney-furniture/rug-rounded kenney-furniture/rug-square kenney-furniture/shower kenney-furniture/shower-round kenney-furniture/stool-bar kenney-furniture/stool-bar-square kenney-furniture/television-antenna kenney-furniture/television-modern kenney-furniture/television-vintage kenney-furniture/toilet kenney-furniture/toilet-square kenney-furniture/trashcan kenney-furniture/wall-doorway kenney-furniture/wall-doorway-wide kenney-furniture/wall-window kenney-furniture/wall-window-slide kenney-nature/plant-bush kenney-nature/plant-bush-detailed kenney-nature/plant-bush-large kenney-nature/plant-bush-large-triangle kenney-nature/plant-bush-small kenney-nature/plant-bush-triangle kenney-nature/plant-flat-short kenney-nature/plant-flat-tall kenney-tiny-dungeon/doorway-rubble kenney-tiny-dungeon/doorway-left kenney-tiny-dungeon/doorway-right kenney-tiny-dungeon/door-open-left kenney-tiny-dungeon/door-open kenney-tiny-dungeon/door-open-right kenney-tiny-dungeon/door-ajar-left kenney-tiny-dungeon/door-ajar kenney-tiny-dungeon/door-ajar-right kenney-tiny-dungeon/door-closed kenney-tiny-dungeon/door-double-left kenney-tiny-dungeon/door-double-right kenney-tiny-dungeon/stool kenney-tiny-town/roof-grey-window kenney-tiny-town/roof-red-window kenney-tiny-town/doorway-wood kenney-tiny-town/doorway-stone kenney-tiny-town/window-wood kenney-tiny-town/door-wood kenney-tiny-town/door-wood-b kenney-tiny-town/door-wood-c kenney-tiny-town/window-stone kenney-tiny-town/door-stone kenney-tiny-town/door-stone-b kenney-tiny-town/door-stone-c kenney-tiny-town/tower-window\nkenney-castle kenney-furniture kenney-mini-dungeon kenney-nature kenney-tiny-dungeon kenney-tiny-town","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"c7aaf4be-b130-4261-b472-a2782ad76c61","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:48:23.297Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== ### loadPack (3022)\n### loadPack()\n\n```ts\nfunction loadPack(url: string, opts: { readonly into?: ModelCatalog; readonly textures?: TextureCatalog } = {}): Promise<ModelCatalog>\n```\n\nLoad a pack of imported models and textures (`public/packs/<pack>.json`, docs/assets/importing.md\n*Packs*) once, the way `loadModel` loads a GLB: the URL resolved the same way (under the\nbase URL; a page may put a data URL for it in `__PIXEL_ASSETS__`, as single-file builds do for\nevery `packs/<id>.json` path the built code names, cut to the models it names), counted by\n`assetProgress`. Resolves to a catalog of the\npack's ModelDefs, to build from with `buildModel(id, { catalog })`; `into` also adds them to a\ncatalog of yours (e.g. `MODEL_LIBRARY`, so `use` finds them), and `textures` gets the pack's\nTextureDefs (e.g. `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`, so `textureMap(id)` and `hudSprite(id)` find them).\n\n### loadPackIndex()\n\n=== ### parsePack (3273)\n### parsePack()\n\n```ts\nfunction parsePack(data: unknown, where = 'pack'): ModelPack\n```\n\nCheck a pack file's shape (the models' and textures' own checks are `validateModel`'s and `validateTexture`'s).\n\n### class PngError\n\nA PNG the decoder can't read, with what is wrong.\n\n- `new PngError(message: string)`\n\n### preloadModels()\n\n```ts\n=== ### setAssetReader (3366)\n### setAssetReader()\n\n```ts\nfunction setAssetReader(read: AssetReader | null): void\n```\n\nWhere models and packs come from, for the whole process (`loadModel` and `loadPack` share one\ncache): a reader, or null for the page's way (fetch under the base URL). Loads already made stay cached.\n\n### interface SheetImport\n\n- `readonly defs: readonly TextureDef[]`\n- `readonly colours: readonly SheetColour[]`: Every distinct opaque source colour of the imported cells, biggest first.\n- `readonly merges: readonly SheetMerge[]`: Every PALETTE entry two or more of those colours bake as, biggest first.\n- `readonly map: ColourMap`: The mapper's result (slots and their entries, before `palette` re-binds them).\n- `readonly cells: readonly SheetCell[]`: Every cell of the grid, in reading order.\n- `readonly columns: number`\n=== ### interface ModelBuild (3094)\n### interface ModelBuild\n\n- `readonly id: string`\n- `readonly object: Group`: Named after the model; pivots are named Groups inside it.\n- `readonly bounds: Bounds`\n- `readonly anchors: Readonly<Record<string, { readonly at: Vec3; readonly rot: Vec3 }>>`\n- `readonly colliders: readonly ColliderData[]`\n- `readonly light: ModelLightRequest | null`\n- `readonly report: ModelReport`\n\n### class ModelCatalog\n\nModels by id: the engine's built-in library (`MODEL_LIBRARY`) or a game's own. `use` parts\nand `buildModel('id')` resolve ids through one (the library unless a build passes another);\na game adds its models to the library, or builds a catalog of its own on top of it.\n\n- `new ModelCatalog(defs: readonly ModelDef[] = [])`\n=== ### hudSprite (2982)\n### hudSprite()\n\n```ts\nfunction hudSprite(idOrDef: string | TextureDef, o: TextureOptions & { frame?: number } = {}): { rows: string[]; colors: Record<string, PaletteColor | number> }\n```\n\nOne frame as `hud.sprite` rows and colours: a character per slot (a, b, c, … in palette order),\n'.' for transparent.\n\n  const s = hudSprite('gem-icon'); hud.sprite(8, 8, s.rows, s.colors, { scale: 2 });\n\n### class ImportError\n\nA file the importer can't read, with what is wrong and what to do.\n\n- `new ImportError(message: string)`\n\n=== ### loadPackIndex (3037)\n### loadPackIndex()\n\n```ts\nfunction loadPackIndex(url = 'packs/index.json'): Promise<PackIndex>\n```\n\nThe packs a site carries (`public/packs/index.json`, written by the importers): each pack's\nid, title, file (relative to the index), how many models and textures it holds, its licence\nand author. Load one with `loadPack(new URL(entry.file, indexUrl))`, or `packs/<file>`.\n\n### meanColour()\n\n```ts\nfunction meanColour(b: BakedTexture): number\n```\n\nThe mean colour of the opaque texels (0xrrggbb, sRGB): what a textured surface reads as from afar.\n=== ### interface HeadlessOptions (305)\n### interface HeadlessOptions\n\n`Engine.headless`: the page's options (those about the page do nothing), and where it runs.\n\n- `viewport?: Viewport`: The viewport the art resolution and framing come from, as a page's would (default 960×540 at DPR 1). Pointer aim and HUD layout depend on it: a replay uses its recording's (`Recording.view`).\n- `assets?: AssetReader`: How models and packs are read: `nodeAssets()` (src/engine/node.ts) reads `public/`.\n\n### class LoadingScreen\n\nMinimal pixel-styled loading indicator: a blocky segmented bar and a status word,\nplain DOM (it shows before the renderer exists). Reuses a `.pixel-loading` element\nalready in the container (index.html ships one so it appears before any JS runs).\n\n- `new LoadingScreen(container: HTMLElement, segments = 12)`\n- `readonly root: HTMLElement`\n- `set(progress: number, label?: string): void`: `progress` 0..1; `label` is shown in capitals.\n- `done(): void`\n=== ### interface TouchButton (2402)\n### interface TouchButton\n\n- `label: string`\n- `code: string`: Key code this button presses (e.g. 'Space').\n- `hint?: string`: Short hint shown under the label.\n- `at?: { x: number; y: number; size?: number; corner?: TouchCorner }`: Place the button yourself instead of in the default grid: its centre, in CSS pixels from `corner` (default bottom-right; `x` grows inward from the side, `y` inward from the top or bottom edge), and its diamet\n\n### interface TouchButtonState\n\nWhat a button shows right now (`TouchControls.set`): a game drives its buttons from its own\nstate each frame (skill icons, cooldowns, costs, a contextual action). Only what changed\ntouches the DOM.\n\n- `label?: string`\n- `hint?: string`\n- `icon?: HTMLCanvasElement | HTMLImageElement | null`: A picture instead of the label (a canvas or image; drawn pixelated); null removes it.\n- `cooldown?: number`: Cooldown shutter, 0..1 of the button covered (0 = ready).\n20:| `roof` | 4.7 × 1.73 × 3.73 | width 4 (1.5–10), depth 3 (1.5–8), pitch 40 (15–60) | tile red, tile2 plum, stone mist, wood orange | architecture, roof, stone, wood | Gable roof to sit on walls (y \n73:| `altar` | 1.9 × 1.02 × 1.12 | w 1.6 (1–2.4) | stone mist, stone2 slate, dark night, cloth red, trim sand | dungeon, stone, cloth, temple | Stone altar on a step: a pale slab top over a dark mould\n75:| `tombstone` | 0.81 × 1.04 × 0.38 | shape 0 (0–2), h 0.9 (0.6–1.3) | stone mist, stone2 slate, carve night, moss green | dungeon, stone, grave | Headstone on a low base with a tuft of moss (map `m\n105\ndoor window doorway wide-window trapdoor stool desk rug folding-screen lamp-post planter kenney-castle/door kenney-castle/tower-square-mid-door kenney-castle/tower-square-mid-windows kenney-castle/tower-square-top-roof-high-windows kenney-castle/wall-doorway kenney-furniture/bathroom-sink kenney-furniture/bathroom-sink-square kenney-furniture/bookcase-closed kenney-furniture/bookcase-closed-doors kenney-furniture/bookcase-closed-wide kenney-furniture/bookcase-open kenney-furniture/bookcase-open-low kenney-furniture/cabinet-television kenney-furniture/cabinet-television-doors kenney-furniture/chair-desk kenney-furniture/coat-rack kenney-furniture/coat-rack-standing kenney-furniture/computer-keyboard kenney-furniture/computer-mouse kenney-furniture/computer-screen kenney-furniture/desk kenney-furniture/desk-corner kenney-furniture/doorway kenney-furniture/doorway-front kenney-furniture/doorway-open kenney-furniture/kitchen-fridge kenney-furniture/kitchen-fridge-built-in kenney-furniture/kitchen-fridge-large kenney-furniture/kitchen-fridge-small kenney-furniture/kit