{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDFXUMfBRnrRiq6UXTR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018Ta6SD5EHNR4L3p9QygpbN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1, (s.count(a),a[:70])\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep('- `hub:session-goal` \"Keep the patient alive and top the team\\'s score\" (≤ 60 chars)','- `hub:session-goal` \"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\" (≤ 60 chars)')\nrep(\"- Saves: guarded `localStorage` under a versioned key. In a session the client hands you an empty store.\",\"- Saves: guarded `localStorage` under a versioned key. In a session the client hands you an empty store.\\n- `game.js` must import cleanly in Node for `check.mjs --headless`: guard `document`, `navigator.getGamepads` and `localStorage`.\")\nrep(\"1. **Skeleton.** Kit, build script, test runner, an empty stage booting from `file://`, music default, input devices with pad stub test.\",\"1. **Skeleton.** Unzip the kit and move the contents of its `pixel-engine/` folder to the dev folder root. `npm install playwright@1.63.0` there. Then: build script, test runner, an empty stage booting from `file://`, music default, input devices with pad stub test.\")\nrep(\"`sixteen_bit` dithers the whole frame and hurts readability ✔.\",\"The split look renders two passes (about a third of the frame rate on software WebGPU here). That's fine: your brief puts performance out of scope. `sixteen_bit` dithers the whole frame and hurts readability ✔.\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 150,215p PLAN.md | cut -c1-260","description":"Apply final corrections and reread the core gameplay section"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6079,"cache_read_input_tokens":474708,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6079},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"c95e2034-ebdb-437d-b7e3-4bf4ee70a5f4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:15:56.752Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDFX3p57nUf2EZdCPPC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018Ta6SD5EHNR4L3p9QygpbN":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211914__x044929/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1, (s.count(a),a[:70])\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep('- `hub:session-goal` \"Keep the patient alive and top the team\\'s score\" (≤ 60 chars)','- `hub:session-goal` \"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\" (≤ 60 chars)')\nrep(\"- Saves: guarded `localStorage` under a versioned key. In a session the client hands you an empty store.\",\"- Saves: guarded `localStorage` under a versioned key. In a session the client hands you an empty store.\\n- `game.js` must import cleanly in Node for `check.mjs --headless`: guard `document`, `navigator.getGamepads` and `localStorage`.\")\nrep(\"1. **Skeleton.** Kit, build script, test runner, an empty stage booting from `file://`, music default, input devices with pad stub test.\",\"1. **Skeleton.** Unzip the kit and move the contents of its `pixel-engine/` folder to the dev folder root. `npm install playwright@1.63.0` there. Then: build script, test runner, an empty stage booting from `file://`, music default, input devices with pad stub test.\")\nrep(\"`sixteen_bit` dithers the whole frame and hurts readability ✔.\",\"The split look renders two passes (about a third of the frame rate on software WebGPU here). That's fine: your brief puts performance out of scope. `sixteen_bit` dithers the whole frame and hurts readability ✔.\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 150,215p PLAN.md | cut -c1-260","description":"Apply final corrections and reread the core gameplay section"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_018Ta6SD5EHNR4L3p9QygpbN":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211914__x044929/work"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018Ta6SD5EHNR4L3p9QygpbN","type":"tool_result","content":"| **Suture** | Zigzag across a wound | A wound has a stitch slot every 0.45. While held, crossing the wound line (amplitude ≥ 0.25) within 0.4 of the next slot ties it. Pitch rises per stitch | Rhythm: 0.2 to 0.7 s per stitch stays CLEAN | Crossing far from th\n| **Laser** | Burn | Hold on a target; heat fills in 0.7 s. Beam, smoke, buzz | Stray time | More than 0.5 s on healthy tissue burns it |\n| **Scanner** | Reveal | Hold; everything hidden within 2.2 units shows and stays marked. A hologram disc shows x-ray silhouettes, with a ping on discovery | Unrated | None |\n| **Gel** | Paint | Hold and sweep a 0.8-radius brush over a mask. Done at 92%. Heals nicks under it after 1 s. In some fights it is a barrier | Speed | None |\n| **Syringe** | Stabilise | Hold 0.45 s to draw, then release inside the glowing injection ring: +18 vitals, −1 dose | Hit the ring | Release outside: dose wasted, SLOPPY |\n\n**Contextual actions** are not on the wheel:\n\n- **Dressing** ends most ops: drag a bandage strip along a marked line.\n- **Paddles** are used in Code Blue (below).\n- **Massage** is used in Op 8.\n\n**Readability at 10 feet:** valid targets for the selected tool pulse softly. A small diamond marks the next task (the hint marker). The hint is on by default, off on Attending, and absent in Op 9. Using the wrong tool on a target gets a tick sound and a Reyes\n\n### Vitals, clock, mistakes\n\n- **Vitals** run 0 to 99 and drain at the op's base rate, plus 0.35/s per open bleeder or pool (capped at 2/s total). Mistakes cost 6.\n- Below 30: red strip, faster EKG beep, Reyes shouts. Below 15: the lamp flickers.\n- **Clock:** reaching 0 fails the op.\n- **Mistakes:** 5 mistakes fail the op (0 in Dev Mode means unlimited).\n- **Failure screen:** flatline, Reyes: \"Time of death...\" Offers **Retry from this stage** (rank capped at B) or **Restart**. After 2 failures, offer to lower the difficulty.\n- **Difficulty:** Intern (time ×1.4, drain ×0.6, two Code Blue saves), Resident (default), Attending (time ×0.8, drain ×1.3, no hint marker).\n\n### Rating and score\n\n- Each completed action rates **CLEAN** (100 points), **GOOD** (60) or **SLOPPY** (20) as a big pop-up near the tip. A **MISTAKE** costs 150.\n- Consecutive CLEANs build a **streak**: +10% per step up to ×2. A rising note scale plays and Reyes comments occasionally. CLEAN also gives +7% Composure.\n- End of op: score plus 5/s of time left, plus 10 per vital point.\n- **Rank** is score against the op's `par`: **S** ≥ 85%, **A** ≥ 70%, **B** ≥ 50%, otherwise **C**. Calibrate `par` from the bot at full skill.\n- **Pristine** is a gold stamp for S with zero mistakes.\n- An unscripted Code Blue caps rank at A.\n\n### The gifts and Composure\n\nComposure is a shared 0 to 100 meter. It starts at 40 and is shown as a bar at top right, hidden until The Quiet awakens in Op 3.\n\n- **The Quiet (Ilya).** Hold L2/Space, needs at least 20%.\n  - The whole sim slows to ×0.25 except cursors, and vitals stop falling.\n  - Composure drains 18%/s of real time.\n  - The picture desaturates, the vignette closes in, and a heartbeat and low drone play. A slow rumble pulses in time.\n- **The Second Look (Sabine).** Press L2/Space, costs 60%.\n  - The sim rewinds 4 s (entities, vitals, mistakes, clock) with a chromatic smear and a tape-rewind whoosh.\n  - The cursor stays where it is, and a translucent ghost hand replays your last 4 s so you can see what went wrong.\n  - It takes 5% off the op's final score. It is disabled during Code Blue.\n  - Implement it by keeping a ring of `structuredClone`s of sim state at 10 Hz; this is why sim state must stay plain data.\n\n✔ Changing a Look's filter parameters is free (frame time unchanged at each `setLook`), so tween `adjust.saturation`, `vignette.intensity` and `chromatic.spread` without a rebuild.\n\n### Code Blue\n\nWhen vitals hit 0 for the first time in an op, the sim freezes, a flatline tone plays and the paddles come up.\n\n- Hold **both triggers** (both mouse buttons; J+K on keyboard) to charge. A needle sweeps up and down over about 1.2 s across a green zone (tunable width 0.2).\n- Release in the zone, on the monitor's beat, for \"CLEAR!\": white flash, thump, hitstop, big rumble.\n- Two good shocks within 12 s return vitals to 25. A bad shock costs 3 s. Run out of time and the patient is lost.\n- Ops can also script a Code Blue (Op 4 teaches it); scripted ones don't cap rank.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Controls and prompts\n\n| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard and mouse |\n|---|---|---|\n| Move instrument | Left stick | Mouse (or WASD/arrows) |\n| Use instrument | R2 (analog: rumble and drain speed follow force), or ✕ | Left click (or J) |\n| Pick tool | Right stick flick: 8 directions, instant, wheel shows while pushed | Number keys 1 to 8, wheel cycles, click the on-screen wheel |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"aaf7edbe-4681-48ea-9de1-c4981bc98a22","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:15:56.787Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"| **Suture** | Zigzag across a wound | A wound has a stitch slot every 0.45. While held, crossing the wound line (amplitude ≥ 0.25) within 0.4 of the next slot ties it. Pitch rises per stitch | Rhythm: 0.2 to 0.7 s per stitch stays CLEAN | Crossing far from th\n| **Laser** | Burn | Hold on a target; heat fills in 0.7 s. Beam, smoke, buzz | Stray time | More than 0.5 s on healthy tissue burns it |\n| **Scanner** | Reveal | Hold; everything hidden within 2.2 units shows and stays marked. A hologram disc shows x-ray silhouettes, with a ping on discovery | Unrated | None |\n| **Gel** | Paint | Hold and sweep a 0.8-radius brush over a mask. Done at 92%. Heals nicks under it after 1 s. In some fights it is a barrier | Speed | None |\n| **Syringe** | Stabilise | Hold 0.45 s to draw, then release inside the glowing injection ring: +18 vitals, −1 dose | Hit the ring | Release outside: dose wasted, SLOPPY |\n\n**Contextual actions** are not on the wheel:\n\n- **Dressing** ends most ops: drag a bandage strip along a marked line.\n- **Paddles** are used in Code Blue (below).\n- **Massage** is used in Op 8.\n\n**Readability at 10 feet:** valid targets for the selected tool pulse softly. A small diamond marks the next task (the hint marker). The hint is on by default, off on Attending, and absent in Op 9. Using the wrong tool on a target gets a tick sound and a Reyes\n\n### Vitals, clock, mistakes\n\n- **Vitals** run 0 to 99 and drain at the op's base rate, plus 0.35/s per open bleeder or pool (capped at 2/s total). Mistakes cost 6.\n- Below 30: red strip, faster EKG beep, Reyes shouts. Below 15: the lamp flickers.\n- **Clock:** reaching 0 fails the op.\n- **Mistakes:** 5 mistakes fail the op (0 in Dev Mode means unlimited).\n- **Failure screen:** flatline, Reyes: \"Time of death...\" Offers **Retry from this stage** (rank capped at B) or **Restart**. After 2 failures, offer to lower the difficulty.\n- **Difficulty:** Intern (time ×1.4, drain ×0.6, two Code Blue saves), Resident (default), Attending (time ×0.8, drain ×1.3, no hint marker).\n\n### Rating and score\n\n- Each completed action rates **CLEAN** (100 points), **GOOD** (60) or **SLOPPY** (20) as a big pop-up near the tip. A **MISTAKE** costs 150.\n- Consecutive CLEANs build a **streak**: +10% per step up to ×2. A rising note scale plays and Reyes comments occasionally. CLEAN also gives +7% Composure.\n- End of op: score plus 5/s of time left, plus 10 per vital point.\n- **Rank** is score against the op's `par`: **S** ≥ 85%, **A** ≥ 70%, **B** ≥ 50%, otherwise **C**. Calibrate `par` from the bot at full skill.\n- **Pristine** is a gold stamp for S with zero mistakes.\n- An unscripted Code Blue caps rank at A.\n\n### The gifts and Composure\n\nComposure is a shared 0 to 100 meter. It starts at 40 and is shown as a bar at top right, hidden until The Quiet awakens in Op 3.\n\n- **The Quiet (Ilya).** Hold L2/Space, needs at least 20%.\n  - The whole sim slows to ×0.25 except cursors, and vitals stop falling.\n  - Composure drains 18%/s of real time.\n  - The picture desaturates, the vignette closes in, and a heartbeat and low drone play. A slow rumble pulses in time.\n- **The Second Look (Sabine).** Press L2/Space, costs 60%.\n  - The sim rewinds 4 s (entities, vitals, mistakes, clock) with a chromatic smear and a tape-rewind whoosh.\n  - The cursor stays where it is, and a translucent ghost hand replays your last 4 s so you can see what went wrong.\n  - It takes 5% off the op's final score. It is disabled during Code Blue.\n  - Implement it by keeping a ring of `structuredClone`s of sim state at 10 Hz; this is why sim state must stay plain data.\n\n✔ Changing a Look's filter parameters is free (frame time unchanged at each `setLook`), so tween `adjust.saturation`, `vignette.intensity` and `chromatic.spread` without a rebuild.\n\n### Code Blue\n\nWhen vitals hit 0 for the first time in an op, the sim freezes, a flatline tone plays and the paddles come up.\n\n- Hold **both triggers** (both mouse buttons; J+K on keyboard) to charge. A needle sweeps up and down over about 1.2 s across a green zone (tunable width 0.2).\n- Release in the zone, on the monitor's beat, for \"CLEAR!\": white flash, thump, hitstop, big rumble.\n- Two good shocks within 12 s return vitals to 25. A bad shock costs 3 s. Run out of time and the patient is lost.\n- Ops can also script a Code Blue (Op 4 teaches it); scripted ones don't cap rank.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Controls and prompts\n\n| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard and mouse |\n|---|---|---|\n| Move instrument | Left stick | Mouse (or WASD/arrows) |\n| Use instrument | R2 (analog: rumble and drain speed follow force), or ✕ | Left click (or J) |\n| Pick tool | Right stick flick: 8 directions, instant, wheel shows while pushed | Number keys 1 to 8, wheel cycles, click the on-screen wheel |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018Ta6SD5EHNR4L3p9QygpbN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDFXUMfBRnrRiq6UXTR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AoqeF1dkiRKYFmNgKGvPMb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211914__x044929/work/planner-exit-interview.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What did you like most about this prompt?\",\n    \"answer\": \"It gives facts I could check instead of guess. The 'This computer' section names the browsers, the WebGPU flags, Playwright's version and what is missing, and the hub link comes with a harness that returns a pass or fail. That let me build small engine spikes and write down verified settings, so builders don't have to rediscover them. I also liked the free choice of genre and perspective alongside firm rules on the things that matter: controller first at 10 feet, attract mode, dev sliders, no stubs.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What was confusing?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Three things. First, 'for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own': it could mean the game only has to keep running outside a session (which is what the hub's check tests) or that it needs its own multiplayer. I planned for both by adding couch co-op. Second, TASK.md is written to a builder (package name, dev folder, chat reply, exit interview) while STAGE.md asks for a plan, so I had to infer which parts bind the planner; I treated them as the builder's. Third, the brief says to prefer file:// while the engine guide says ES modules don't load from file://. Inlining the module resolves this, but I only knew that after testing it.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What was the hardest thing to do?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Keeping the game original while still capturing the source. Much of what makes the source recognisable is its names, plot and specific operations, and the plan has to avoid all of those yet keep its feel, so I had to invent a new world, cast, disease and boss designs that still feel like the same genre and tone. A close second was scoping: the plan had to be large enough to show every mechanic but still buildable by agents I can't answer questions for, which is why it has a build order and an explicit cut order.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What would you change in this prompt?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Mark which sections apply to the planner and which to the builder. Define 'on its own' in one sentence. Say how long or detailed a plan should be, and whether engine spikes are welcome and where scratch files may go. Add -u to the example server command: `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` doesn't flush its port line into a pipe, and a script reading it hangs, which cost me about ten minutes. It would also help to warn that the engine's bundled hero is a red-capped plumber, because 'use the native style' invites using it until you actually look at it.\"\n  }\n]\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6079,"cache_read_input_tokens":474708,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6079},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b716b92-81c2-4c62-8381-9131b2f861f1","uuid":"2f21b64e-4eb8-4834-8096-8692c633008e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:16:05.997Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDFX3p57nUf2EZdCPPC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AoqeF1dkiRKYFmNgKGvPMb":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211914__x044929/work/planner-exit-interview.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What did you like most about this prompt?\",\n    \"answer\": \"It gives facts I could check instead of guess. The 'This computer' section names the browsers, the WebGPU flags, Playwright's version and what is missing, and the hub link comes with a harness that returns a pass or fail. That let me build small engine spikes and write down verified settings, so builders don't have to rediscover them. I also liked the free choice of genre and perspective alongside firm rules on the things that matter: controller first at 10 feet, attract mode, dev sliders, no stubs.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What was confusing?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Three things. First, 'for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own': it could mean the game only has to keep running outside a session (which is what the hub's check tests) or that it needs its own multiplayer. I planned for both by adding couch co-op. Second, TASK.md is written to a builder (package name, dev folder, chat reply, exit interview) while STAGE.md asks for a plan, so I had to infer which parts bind the planner; I treated them as the builder's. Third, the brief says to prefer file:// while the engine guide says ES modules don't load from file://. Inlining the module resolves this, but I only knew that after testing it.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What was the hardest thing to do?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Keeping the game original while still capturing the source. Much of what makes the source recognisable is its names, plot and specific operations, and the plan has to avoid all of those yet keep its feel, so I had to invent a new world, cast, disease and boss designs that still feel like the same genre and tone. A close second was scoping: the plan had to be large enough to show every mechanic but still buildable by agents I can't answer questions for, which is why it has a build order and an explicit cut order.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What would you change in this prompt?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Mark which sections apply to the planner and which to the builder. Define 'on its own' in one sentence. Say how long or detailed a plan should be, and whether engine spikes are welcome and where scratch files may go. Add -u to the example server command: `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` doesn't flush its port line into a pipe, and a script reading it hangs, which cost me about ten minutes. It would also help to warn that the engine's bundled hero is a red-capped plumber, because 'use the native style' invites using it until you actually look at it.\"\n  }\n]\n"}}}
